('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078-quantitative-approach', 'Quantitative methods (working with numbers)', 'Quantitative research uses numbers to describe or compare patterns—for example, counting how often students report using a library. The design and sample determine what the numbers can support.', 'Choose this approach when a question needs numerical measurement, counting, comparison or a statistical summary; it is an option, not a requirement for every route.', 'A small, clearly labelled table or chart with a cautious interpretation; illustrative practice only.', 'build_next', 'Choose this approach when a question needs numerical measurement, counting, comparison or a statistical summary; it is an option, not a requirement for every route. Do not imply every social researcher must use statistics or that numerical results automatically establish causation, representativeness or meaning. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['unesco_definition', 'nuc_ccmas', 'openlearn_jamovi']::text[], '[{"id":"unesco_definition","title":"Social science research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/query-list/s/social-science-research","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"nuc_ccmas","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"D078_checkpoint_context_candidate"},{"id":"openlearn_jamovi","title":"Getting started with Jamovi","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"unesco_definition","title":"Social science research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/query-list/s/