('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078-survey-method', 'Surveys and questionnaire design', 'A survey asks people a planned set of questions so answers can be compared. Clear wording, suitable response options, testing and sampling matter; a survey form alone does not make results representative.', 'Use a survey when planned questions to a defined group can answer the research question; choose wording, response options and sampling to fit the intended conclusion.', 'A short draft questionnaire with a pretest plan; use fictional/sample respondents unless the needed permissions and review are in place.', 'build_next', 'Use a survey when planned questions to a defined group can answer the research question; choose wording, response options and sampling to fit the intended conclusion. A questionnaire or large response count does not by itself make results representative or unbiased; preserve sampling, nonresponse and wording limits. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['apsa_2024', 'pew_survey']::text[], '[{"id":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"pew_survey","title":"Writing Survey Questions","url":"https://www.pewresearch.org/writing-survey-questions/","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","locator":"pri