epresentative or unbiased; preserve sampling, nonresponse and wording limits. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.'),
('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078-interviews', 'Interviews', 'An interview is a planned conversation for learning how someone understands or experiences an issue. It can add depth, but does not automatically measure how common an experience is.', 'Use interviews when the question needs detailed accounts, views or experiences; interview findings alone do not show how common a view is.', 'A draft topic guide and an explanation of how each question relates to the study question; do not interview real people without approval/permissions.', 'build_next', 'Use interviews when the question needs detailed accounts, views or experiences; interview findings alone do not show how common a view is. An interview account is not automatically a verified fact or representative view; consent, power, recall, interviewer influence and analysis must be considered. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['apsa_2024', 'openlearn_interviews']::text[], '[{"id":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"openlearn_interviews","title":"Conducting qualitative interviews: an introduction","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/conducting-qualitative-interviews-introduction/content-section-0","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","locator":"printed p. 22: interviews as one commonly deployed method","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","locator":"printed p. 22: interviews as one commonly deployed method","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"openlearn_interviews","title":"Conducting qualitative interviews: an introduction","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/conducting-qualitative-interviews-introduction/content-section-0","locator":"Course introduction and sections on preparation, conducting and recording qualitative interviews.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Interview answers are context-dependent; do not generalize prevalence from a small purposive group.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/conducting-qualitative-interviews-introduction/content-section-0', 'Open: Conducting qualitative interviews: an introduction', '{"source_id":"openlearn_interviews","title":"Open: Conducting qualitative interviews: an introduction","publisher":null,"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/conducting-qualitative-interviews-introduction/content-section-0","locator":"Course content: 1.1 when interviews are useful; 2.1–2.5 preparation and ethics; 3.1–3.4 asking questions, consent and ending; 4.1–4.5 fieldnotes and data handling.","accessed_on":"2026-10-08","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-08', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/conducting-qualitative-interviews-introduction/content-section-0","locator":"Course content: 1.1 when 