('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078-document-analysis', 'Document and content analysis', 'Document/content analysis uses a planned way to examine texts or records—for example, comparing how a policy describes access across editions. The material and coding rules must fit the question.', 'Use this when existing documents or records are evidence for the question; define which materials count and how they will be examined or coded.', 'A small code/category list and a documented sample analysis using public or fictional documents.', 'build_next', 'Use this when existing documents or records are evidence for the question; define which materials count and how they will be examined or coded. Software highlighting or tagging is not the method itself; distinguish descriptive content coding from discourse, conversation or other specialist analyses. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['apsa_2024', 'taguette_tutorial', 'url_a40c57828378bb4d']::text[], '[{"id":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinking Political Science Education: Presidential Task Force Report","url":"https://educate.apsanet.org/wp-content/uploads/APSA-Presidential-Task-Force-Report-on-Rethinking-Political-Science-Education-March-2024.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"taguette_tutorial","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"},{"id":"url_a40c57828378bb4d","title":"Learn how social researchers use and analyse documents","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/education-development/postgraduate-studies/defining-your-research-methodology","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"apsa_2024","title":"Rethinki