('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078-observation-ethnography', 'Observation and ethnographic approaches', 'Observation records what happens in a setting; ethnographic approaches study practices and meaning in context over time. For example, a researcher might observe how people use a public service, then keep field notes about what happened and the setting. Work with real people needs a clear purpose, permission and safeguards.', 'Use observation when practices or interactions need to be studied in their setting, and an ethnographic approach when meaning and context over time matter; plan permissions and safeguards for real people.', 'A short observation guide and sample field notes from a public/fictional scenario, with a reflection on what the researcher could and could not conclude.', 'build_next', 'Use observation when practices or interactions need to be studied in their setting, and an ethnographic approach when meaning and context over time matter; plan permissions and safeguards for real people. Ethnography is not simply watching people. Researcher position, access, consent, privacy, field records and interpretation require careful treatment. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['unesco_isced_detail', 'openlearn_social_participation']::text[], '[{"id":"unesco_isced_detail","title":"ISCED-F 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://www.uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"openlearn_social_participation","title":"Social science and participation: Participating in social science","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/social-science-and-participation/content-section-4","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"unesco_isced_detail","title":"ISCED-F 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://www.uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","locator":"field 0314 sociology/anthropology field boundaries","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"unesco_isced_detail","title":"ISCED-F 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://www.uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","locator":"field 0314 sociology/anthropology field boundaries","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"openlearn_social_participation","title":"Social science and participation: Participating in social science","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/social-science-and-participation/content-section-4","locator":"Section ''Participating in social science'', especially the table at lines 168–182: explains how social scientists interact with participants and names surveys, focus groups, qualitative interviews, ethnographic observation and quantitative measurement. Course metadata at lines 97–103: free, Level 2 intermediate, 10 hours.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Not needed for every social-science path; observation and ethnography vary by discipline, purpose and setting.","The OpenLearn ethnography resource is Level 3 advanced and organisationally situated; the Level 2 course section is broader but not comprehensive fieldwork training.","Do not observe people covertly or treat a practice example as permission to conduct real-world research.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/social-science-and-participation/content-section-4', 'Open: Social science and participation: Participating in social science', '{"source_id":"openlearn_social_participation","title":"Open: Social science and participation: Participating in social science","publisher":null,"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/social-science-and-participation/content-section-4","locator":"Section table ‘Forms of participation in social science methodologies’, including experiments, surveys, focus groups, qualitative interviews, ethnographic observation and quantitative measurement.","accessed_on":"2026-10-08","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-08', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/social-science-and-participation/content-section-4","locator":"Section table ‘Forms of participation in social science methodologies’, including experiments, surveys, focus groups, qualitative interviews, ethnographic observation and quantitative measurement.","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":"Free OpenLearn course; account/sign-in for course completion record"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"unesco_isced_detail","title":"ISCED-F 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://www.uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"unesco_isced_detail","title":"ISCED-F 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://www.uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-f