('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-qualitative-coding-tool', 'Taguette for highlighting and coding documents', 'Taguette lets a learner highlight passages in documents, attach codes and retrieve coded excerpts. The researcher still decides what the codes mean and whether the interpretation is justified.', 'Use Taguette when a qualitative document workflow benefits from highlighting, tagging and retrieving passages; manual coding with a documented process is also valid.', 'A short codebook and tagged sample using public or fictional text.', 'build_next', 'Use Taguette when a qualitative document workflow benefits from highlighting, tagging and retrieving passages; manual coding with a documented process is also valid. Tags do not generate defensible themes by themselves; a codebook, interpretation, context and reflexive decisions remain the researcher''s responsibility. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['taguette_tutorial']::text[], '[{"id":"taguette_tutorial","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"taguette_tutorial","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","locator":"official walkthrough: project, documents, highlights/tags, export","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"taguette_tutorial","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","locator":"official walkthrough: project, documents, highlights/tags, export","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"taguette_tutorial","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","locator":"Walkthrough: create a project, upload documents, high