('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-spss-tool', 'SPSS for statistical analysis when the project calls for it', 'SPSS is software for preparing and analysing structured data—for example, producing a frequency table or testing a relationship between measured variables. The researcher still chooses a method that fits the question, checks its assumptions and explains the result; SPSS does not make an analysis valid by itself.', 'Can execute selected quantitative procedures on appropriately prepared social/behavioural data; method selection and interpretation remain researcher responsibilities.', 'A simple analysis of sample or fictional data, with a saved output table/chart and a plain-language explanation of the procedure and its limits.', 'build_next', 'Can execute selected quantitative procedures on appropriately prepared social/behavioural data; method selection and interpretation remain researcher responsibilities. Do not require SPSS alongside R, Python or other packages by default; software output does not validate design, measurement, assumptions or interpretation. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ibm_spss_resources', 'url_9d89365e19fae3a4']::text[], '[{"id":"ibm_spss_resources","title":"Resources for IBM SPSS Statistics","url":"https://www.ibm.com/products/spss-statistics/resources","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"url_9d89365e19fae3a4","title":"Open University OpenLearn","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/sociology/getting-started-spss/content-section-0?active-tab=description-tab","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"ibm_spss_resources","title":"Resources for IBM SPSS Statistics","url":"https://www.ibm.com/products/spss-statistics/resources","locat