pport a documented qualitative workflow when a D078 question uses interviews, open responses, documents or multimedia; the researcher still defines the question, sampling, coding logic and interpretation. NVivo does not perform interpretation on the researcher''s behalf, establish a valid theme, choose the method or remove software-access and licensing constraints. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.'),
('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-pandas-tool', 'pandas for cleaning and combining tabular research data', 'pandas is a Python library for working with tables, such as survey answers or public statistics. It can help read files, check and change columns, summarize values, and combine tables. It does not decide whether the questions, sample or conclusions are sound.', 'Supports preparation and summary of tabular social data such as survey/administrative tables; it does not decide what variables mean.', 'A reproducible notebook that reads a permitted practice dataset, documents cleaning decisions, produces a summary table, and records limitations.', 'build_next', 'Supports preparation and summary of tabular social data such as survey/administrative tables; it does not decide what variables mean. It is a data-handling library, not a research method or statistical-validity guarantee; Python programming and data concepts are prerequisites to using it well. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['pandas_tutorials', 'url_4971ef18227673ce']::text[], '[{"id":"pandas_tutorials","title":"Getting started tutorials","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/getting_started/intro_tutorials/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"url_4971ef18227673ce","title":"Data Carpentry","url":"https://datacarpentry.org/python-socialsci/","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"pandas_tutorials","title":"Getting started tutorials","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/getting_started/intro_tutorials/index.html","locator":"official tutorials for tabular data import, selection, summaries, reshaping and joining","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"pandas_tutorials","title":"Getting started tutorials","url":"