('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-matplotlib-tool', 'Matplotlib for creating Python charts', 'Matplotlib is a Python library for making charts. For example, a researcher can turn a checked table into a labelled chart that helps readers compare groups or values. The chart still needs accurate data, a fair scale and a clear explanation.', 'Use Matplotlib when a Python workflow needs a clearly labelled chart from prepared data; charting does not validate the data, analysis or interpretation.', 'One clearly labelled chart made from a permitted practice dataset, with a short note about the comparison and what it cannot show.', 'build_next', 'Use Matplotlib when a Python workflow needs a clearly labelled chart from prepared data; charting does not validate the data, analysis or interpretation. Charting does not validate data, justify a chart type or support causal conclusions; visual choices can mislead if context is omitted. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['matplotlib_getting_started']::text[], '[{"id":"matplotlib_getting_started","title":"Getting started","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/users/getting_started/","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"matplotlib_getting_started","title":"Getting started","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/users/getting_started/","locator":"official guide installs the package and demonstrates drawing a plot","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"matplotlib_getting_started","title":"Getting started","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/users/getting_started/","locator":"official guide installs the package and demonstrates drawing a plot","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"matplotlib_getting_started","title":"Getting started","url":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/users/getting_