('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-networkx-tool', 'NetworkX for analysing relationship data as a graph', 'NetworkX is a Python library for representing relationships as a graph: people or organisations become points, and recorded connections become lines. It can calculate network measures and apply graph algorithms. It cannot tell you whether the recorded ties are complete or what a measure means socially without a sound research design and interpretation.', 'Can help analyse social ties, communication, collaboration or other relational structures when the research design and network data define what nodes/edges mean.', 'A small, anonymised practice network with a documented definition of a node and tie, one justified network measure, and a note about missing/biased ties and interpretation limits.', 'useful_later', 'Can help analyse social ties, communication, collaboration or other relational structures when the research design and network data define what nodes/edges mean. Graph algorithms do not explain why relationships exist or prove influence; network boundaries, missing ties and measurement choices shape the results. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['networkx_tutorial', 'url_e3b57ac49003d3bb']::text[], '[{"id":"networkx_tutorial","title":"Tutorial","url":"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/tutorial.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"url_e3b57ac49003d3bb","title":"NetworkX project","url":"https://networkx.org/nx-guides/content/exploratory_notebooks/facebook_notebook.html","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"networkx_tutorial","title":"Tutorial","url":"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/tutorial.html","locator":"official tutorial covers graph creation, nodes, edges, attributes, algorithms and drawing","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"networkx_tutorial","title":"Tutorial","url":"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/tutorial.html","locator":"official tutorial covers graph creation, nodes, edges, attributes, algorithms and drawing","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"networkx_tutorial","title":"Tutorial","url":"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/tutorial.html","locator":"Official tutorial sections on graph creation, nodes/edges, graph types, attributes, algorithms, drawing and input/output; graph concepts and algorithms are made available through Python APIs.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Belongs only to a network-analysis route, not every D078 learner or every computational-social-science project.","Relationship data can expose sensitive information; use privacy-preserving practice data and appropriate ethics review.","For large graphs, performance and alternative platforms need separate assessment.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://networkx.org/nx-guides/content/exploratory_notebooks/facebook_notebook.html', 'NetworkX project', '{"source_id":"url_e3b57ac49003d3bb","title":"NetworkX project","publisher":"NetworkX project","url":"https://networkx.org/nx-guides/content/exploratory_notebooks/facebook_notebook.html","locator":"Hands-on social-network analysis notebook; free and directly task-specific","accessed_on":"2026-10-09","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-09', 'medium', '{"url":"https://networkx.org/nx-guides/content/exploratory_notebooks/facebook_notebook.html","locator":"Hands-on social-network analysis notebook; free and directly task-specific","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":null}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_i