ction/visualization tutorials","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]},"expected_output":{"source_references":[{"id":"mesa_first_model","title":"Creating Your First Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"D078_checkpoint_context_candidate"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"mesa_first_model","title":"Creating Your First Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"official getting-started tutorial builds a basic model and links data-collection/visualization tutorials","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"d078-mesa-tool"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Open resource; check the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'specialist_tool_for_agent_based_modelling', 'Specialist tool for agent based modelling', 'specialist_tool_for_agent_based_modelling', 'optional', 'Can operationalise a stated social mechanism as interacting simulated agents and support scenario exploration; it is a model-building tool, not evidence by itself. Mesa helps implement a model; it does not validate assumptions or make simulated outcomes observations of real society. Python and modelling concepts precede tool operation. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.'),
('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-casevo-tool', 'Casevo for cognitive-agent social-simulation experiments', 'Casevo is a specialist Python framework for multi-agent social-simulation experiments on complex networks. Its project tutorial combines Mesa-based simulation, NetworkX graphs, Matplotlib, and an LLM interface. This can be explored only when a well-defined research question specifically calls for this kind of model; it is not a required step after learning Python or a general replacement for research with people or observed data.', 'A specialist option for formalising a social-process theory as a simulation; not a substitute for observed community or participant evidence.', 'A small model-comparison notebook that states what agents represent, what assumptions/prompts and network rules were used, how outputs were checked, and why simulation results cannot be treated as real-world findings without validation.', 'useful_later', 'A specialist option for formalising a social-process theory as a simulation; not a substitute for observed community or participant evidence. It is not a generic case-study tool, a substitute for empirical participant evidence, or a validated forecasting system. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['casevo_readme_tutorial']::text[], '[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1–4: project describes a Python framework for social-simulation multi-agent experiments on complex networks; says it is built on Mesa; tutorial incrementally builds a basic model and simple result analysis. Sections 4.1–4.3 demonstrate a network configuration using NetworkX and Matplotlib and an LLM API integration. Repository notes Python >3.11; 0.3.19 release dated 2025-04-22; Apache-2.0 license.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Emerging/niche project candidate; do not promote as a common or established D078 tool without further adoption/maintenance evidence.","Project example uses U.S. election data/personas; it is illustrative, not Nigeria-specific validation.","LLM-generated agent conversations or choices are simulated outputs, not representative human responses or evidence of actual social behavior.","Version and third-party LLM dependencies can change; recheck before any student link is published.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo', 'Casevo project', '{"source_id":"url_1f481c25128b1853","title":"Casevo project","publisher":"Casevo project","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README tutorial: incrementally build and analyse a basic social simulation","accessed_on":"2026-10-09","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-09', 'medium', '{"url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README tutorial: incrementally build and analyse a basic social simulation","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":null}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"item_identity"}]},"checkpoint_fit":{"source_references":[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"D078_checkpoint_context_candidate"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1–4: project describes a Python framework for social-simulation multi-agent experiments on complex networks; says it is built on Mesa; tutorial incrementally builds a basic model and simple result analysis. Sections 4.1–4.3 demonstrate a network configuration using NetworkX and Matplotlib and an LLM API integration. Repository notes Python >3.11; 0.3.19 release dated 2025-04-22; Apache-2.0 license.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"D078_checkpoint_context_candidate"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]},"expected_output":{"source_references":[{"id":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":"D078_checkpoint_context_candidate"}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"casevo_readme_tutorial","title":"Casevo: Cognitive agents and social evolution simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"project README identifies use case, Mesa basis, NetworkX/Matplotlib example, LLM integration, Python version and tutorial","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"d078-casevo-tool"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Open resource; check the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'emerging_specialist_candidate_under_review', 'Emerging specialist candidate under review', 'emerging_specialist_candidate_under_review', 'optional', 'A specialist option for formalising a social-process theory as a simulation; not a substitute for observed community or participant evidence. It is not a generic case-study tool, a substitute for empirical participant evidence, or a validated forecasting system. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.'),
('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'competency', 'sampling_recruitment_and_representativeness', 'Sampling and knowing what evidence represents', 'Choose people, cases or datasets carefully and explain which wider group the evidence can and cannot represent.', 'Select or assess participants, cases or datasets and state what the evidence can represent.', 'A short sampling or case-selection plan that names the population, selection approach and important limits.', 'build_next', 'Select or assess participants, cases or datasets and state what the evidence can represent. Keep probability-sample representativeness distinct from purposive case selection. A case or convenience sample must not be described as representing a wider population without design support. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['aapor_best_practices_sampling', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'open_text_sampling_ch8', 'ukds_intro_survey_data']::text[], '[{"id":"aapor_best_practices_sampling","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research — Designing Your Sample","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"open_text_sampling_ch8","title":"Social Science Research: Princip