('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'measurement_and_operationalisation', 'Turning ideas into observable measures', 'Turn an idea such as trust, wellbeing or access into questions, observations or records that can be examined, while explaining what the measure leaves out.', 'Turn ideas such as trust or wellbeing into observable measures and explain their limits.', 'A small measurement plan showing the concept, indicators, questions or observations, and their limitations.', 'build_next', 'Turn ideas such as trust or wellbeing into observable measures and explain their limits. Do not imply that every social concept must be reduced to a numeric measure or that operationalisation replaces qualitative interpretation. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['gesis_survey_instruments_measurement', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'open_text_measurement_ch6', 'macewan_social_research_measurement_ch4']::text[], '[{"id":"gesis_survey_instruments_measurement","title":"Survey Instruments","url":"https://www.gesis.org/en/gesis-guides/gesis-survey-guides/instruments","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"open_text_measurement_ch6","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practi