3-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","locator":"Annex I, printed p. 22 (social-science researcher learning outcomes); Annex II, printed p. 23 (research questions, qualitative/quantitative methods, sampling and case selection, generalisability, validity, reliability and replicability).","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","locator":"Printed pp. 177–178, Sociology Research Method II (proposal, data collection/organisation, pilot study, report and statistics); printed p. 214, Political Science research methods (research questions, instruments, data collection and analysis).","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"focus_groups_and_workshops"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', 'Introductory-to-intermediate', 'English', 'Free online guide', NULL, 'conditional_method_choice', 'Conditional method choice', 'conditional_method_choice', 'useful', 'Study how people discuss a topic together and how group interaction shapes evidence. Not a universal interview substitute; a group discussion does not produce representative views by default. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for e