('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'discourse_and_conversation_analysis', 'Discourse and conversation analysis', 'Study how language is used to construct meaning, identity, relationships or social positions, and how conversation is organised turn by turn.', 'Study language, interaction, framing and social practice rather than only topics.', 'A carefully selected and transcribed extract with an analytic account of wording, sequence, interaction and the limits of the interpretation.', 'useful_later', 'Study language, interaction, framing and social practice rather than only topics. Do not confuse topic coding or word counts with discourse/conversation analysis; each requires a defined analytic framework. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['uni_ni_discourse_conversation_definition_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'nou_conversation_analysis_courseware_2026', 'casrai_discourse_analysis_guide_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"uni_ni_discourse_conversation_definition_2026","title":"Qualitative Data: Discourse Analysis and Conversation Analysis","url":"https://researchmethods.uni.edu/chapter-five-qualitative-methods/chapter-five-qualitative-data-part-2","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},