('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'case_study_and_comparative_case_design', 'Case-study and comparative-case design', 'Study one or a small number of bounded real-world cases in depth, or compare cases deliberately to understand similarities, differences and possible explanations.', 'Set defensible boundaries around a case and compare cases without treating one example as universal.', 'A case-selection and evidence plan that states the case boundary, comparison logic, sources, rival explanations and what cannot be generalised.', 'build_next', 'Set defensible boundaries around a case and compare cases without treating one example as universal. Do not imply one case represents all cases or that case study is only qualitative; explain the design and inference it supports. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['rug_case_research_definition_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'taso_comparative_case_study_2026', 'url_cac4dec9111d7ff1']::text[], '[{"id":"rug_case_research_definition_2026","title":"Case Research","url":"https://opentextbooks.rug.nl/rspremsc/chapter/case-research/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"taso_comparative_case_study_2026","title":"Comparative case stu