('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'archival_and_historical_research', 'Archival and historical research', 'Use records from archives and historical collections to investigate people, institutions or events while checking provenance, context, gaps and preservation limits.', 'Use records and archives as evidence while checking provenance, context and gaps.', 'A source log that records where each record came from, what it can show, missing material and why it is used for the question.', 'build_next', 'Use records and archives as evidence while checking provenance, context and gaps. Do not present interview-method sources as proof of archival practice; preserve the source-coverage gap. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['leicester_archival_research_guide_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'ipsrm_archival_research_explanation_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"leicester_archival_research_guide_2026","title":"Doing archival research","url":"https://le.ac.uk/history/outreach/besh/historical-research/archival-research","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"ipsrm_archival_research_explanation_2026","title":"Archival Research","url":"https://ipsrm.com/ipsrm/chapter/13","region":null,"evid