('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'participatory_and_action_research', 'Participatory and action research', 'Work with people affected by an issue so they can help shape the question, evidence, interpretation and possible action rather than being treated only as subjects.', 'Involve affected communities in framing questions, design, interpretation or action.', 'A participation plan showing who has influence at each stage, how decisions are recorded, what action follows and how power, consent and disagreement are handled.', 'build_next', 'Involve affected communities in framing questions, design, interpretation or action. Do not label ordinary consultation as participatory/action research; address consent, ownership, safety and expectations of impact. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['mit_par_definition_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'kyoto_par_methods_explanation_2026', 'url_cac4dec9111d7ff1']::text[], '[{"id":"mit_par_definition_2026","title":"Practice of Participatory Action Research","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-237-practice-of-participatory-action-research-par-spring-2016/resources/11-237s162/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"kyoto_par_methods_explanation_2026","title":"Basic Theory and Methods of Participatory Action Research","url":"https://ocw.kyoto-u.ac.jp/en/course/227/?video_id=3168","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_cac4dec9111d7ff1","title":"Learn participatory action research methods","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-237-practice-of-participatory-action-research-par-spring-2016/pages/calendar/","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"mit_par_definition_2026","title":"Practice of Participatory Action Research","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/11-237-practice-of-participatory-action-research-par-spring-2016/resources/11-237s162/","locator":"Course description defining PAR as producing actionable knowledge communities can use","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","locator":"Annex I, printed p. 22 (social-science researcher learning outcomes); Annex II, printed p. 23 (research questions, qualitative/quantitative methods, sampling and case selection, generalisability, validity, reliability and replicability).","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","locator":"Printed pp. 177–178, Sociology Research Method II (proposal, data collection/organisation, pilot study, report and statistics); printed p. 214, Political Science research methods (research questions, instruments, data collection and analysis).","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"kyoto_par_methods_explanation_2026","title":"Basic Theory and Methods of Participatory Action Research","url":"https://ocw.kyoto-u.ac.