('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'experiments_quasi_experiments_and_causal_inference', 'Experiments, quasi-experiments and causal inference', 'Design comparisons that help estimate whether an intervention or exposure contributed to an outcome, while making the assumptions and possible confounding visible.', 'Distinguish association from causal effect using design, comparison and explicit assumptions.', 'A design note naming the treatment/exposure, comparison, outcome, timing, identification assumptions, threats to validity and limits of the causal claim.', 'useful_later', 'Distinguish association from causal effect using design, comparison and explicit assumptions. Association, prediction and before/after change alone do not establish causation; do not imply every D078 role runs experiments. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ucla_methods_matter_causal_inference_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'duke_causal_inference_tutorial_2026', 'causal_inference_mixtape_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"ucla_methods_matter_causal_inference_2026","title":"Methods Matter: Improving Causal Inference in Educational and Social Science Research","url":"https://stats.oarc.ucla.edu/other/examples/methods-matter/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-F