('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'psychometrics_and_scale_construction', 'Psychometrics and scale construction', 'Turn an abstract construct into a set of items or indicators, then test whether the scale behaves consistently and supports the intended interpretation for the population studied.', 'Develop and assess multi-item measures for behavioural and social constructs.', 'A construct definition, item-development record, pilot results and reliability/validity evidence with limits and any group-specific validation needs.', 'useful_later', 'Develop and assess multi-item measures for behavioural and social constructs. Not required for all behavioural/social research; reliability alone does not validate a scale for a population. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['pmc_scale_development_primer_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'sophia_scale_construction_tutorial_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"pmc_scale_development_primer_2026","title":"Best Practices for Developing and Validating Scales for Health, Social, and Behavioral Research","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6004510/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"sophia_scale_construction_tutorial_2026","title":"S