('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'longitudinal_panel_and_multilevel_data', 'Longitudinal, panel and multilevel data', 'Analyse data collected repeatedly over time or collected in groups within groups, while accounting for the dependence and structure those designs create.', 'Analyse people over time or people nested within schools, households, communities or other groups.', 'A data-structure and analysis plan identifying units, time points, levels, missingness, model assumptions and the limits of the conclusions.', 'useful_later', 'Analyse people over time or people nested within schools, households, communities or other groups. Repeated observations or grouped data do not automatically justify a causal or multilevel model. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ucla_longitudinal_multilevel_definition_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'vu_panel_multilevel_explanation_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"ucla_longitudinal_multilevel_definition_2026","title":"Analyzing Longitudinal Data using Multilevel Modeling","url":"https://stats.oarc.ucla.edu/other/mult-pkg/seminars/mlm-longitudinal/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"vu_panel_multilevel_explanation_2026","title":"Tutorial in Multilevel Models","url":"https://research.vu.nl/en/courses/tutorial-in-multilevel-models/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"ucla_longitudinal_multilevel_definition_2026","title":"Analyzing Longitudinal Data using Multilevel Modeling","url":"https://stats.oarc.ucla.edu/other/mult-pkg/seminars/mlm-longitudinal/","locator":"Description of repeated observations, longitudinal outcomes and multilevel approaches","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","locator":"Annex I, printed p. 22 (social-science researcher learning outcomes); Annex II, printed p. 23 (research questions, qualitative/quantitative methods, sampling and case selection, generalisability, validity, reliability and replicability).","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Social-Sciences-CCMAS-FINAL-2023-A.pdf","locator":"Printed pp. 177–178, Sociology Research Method II (proposal, data collection/organisation, pilot study, report and statistics); printed p. 214, Political Science research methods (research questions, instruments, data collection and analysis).","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"vu_panel_multilevel_explanation_2026","title":"Tutorial in Multilevel Models","url":"https://research.vu.nl/en/courses/tutorial-in-multilevel-models/","locator":"Course objectives and explanation of clustered and panel data","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A sophisticated model cannot repair poor measurement, missing data or an unsuitable research design.","Repeated observations and clustered data require assumptions that should be explained rat