('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'systematic_and_scoping_evidence_synthesis', 'Evidence synthesis: systematic reviews and scoping reviews', 'Evidence synthesis uses a documented method to find, select, assess and bring together existing studies. A systematic review answers a focused question using predefined methods; a scoping review maps what evidence or concepts exist and where evidence gaps may be. They are related but not interchangeable.', 'Find, screen, assess and combine existing studies rather than collecting new data by default.', 'A documented question and review type, protocol or plan, search record, study-selection decisions, evidence summary and limitations appropriate to the chosen review method.', 'build_next', 'Find, screen, assess and combine existing studies rather than collecting new data by default. Do not call a general literature search a systematic/scoping review without appropriate transparent methods. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024', 'campbell_oli_systematic_review_free_course']::text[], '[{"id":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","title":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","url":"https://jbi-global-wiki.refined.site/download/attachments/355599504/JBI%20Manual%20for%20Evidence%20Synthesis%202024.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":"item_definition_or_task_identity"},{"id":"campbell_oli_systematic_review_free_course","title":"Learn systematic-review methods for social-science research (advanced)","url":"https://oli.cmu.edu/courses/systematic-reviews-and-meta-analysis-o-f/","region":null,"evidenceType":"independent_or_task_specific_explanation_candidate"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","title":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","url":"https://jbi-global-wiki.refined.site/download/attachments/355599504/JBI%20Manual%20for%20Evidence%20Synthesis%202024.pdf","locator":"Chapter 1, printed pp. 5–6: evidence-synthesis types and JBI approach; Chapter 10, printed pp. 162 onward: scoping-review purpose, question, protocol and methods. JBI advises cross-checking the online manual because the PDF may not contain later updates.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","title":"jbi_manual_evidence_synthesis_2024","url":"https://jbi-global-wiki.refined.site/download/attachments/355599504/JBI%20Manual%20for%20Evidence%20Synthesis%202024.pdf","locator":"Chapter 1, printed pp. 5–6: evidence-synthesis types and JBI approach; Chapter 10, printed pp. 162 onward: scoping-review purpose, question, protocol and methods. JBI advises cross-checking the online manual because the PDF may not contain later updates.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"campbell_oli_systematic_review_free_course","title":"Learn systematic-review methods for social-science research (advanced)","url":"https://oli.cmu.edu/courses/systematic-reviews-and-meta-analysis-o-f/","locator":"Modules 1–15 cover review scope, questions, searches, screening and recording; modules 16–28 cover selection, coding, appraisal and software. The course is Open & Free for independent learners.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Evidence synthesis is relevant to selected research, policy and practice tasks, not every D078 role or project.","PRISMA is a reporting guideline, not a complete conduct method.","The Campbell course focuses on systematic reviews and meta-analysis and is advanced; it does not teach scoping review as a beginner pathway.","The JBI manual is formal method guidance, not an introductory course and is specifically grounded in JBI methods.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked'