('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'competency', 'ai_assisted_and_digital_trace_research_ethics', 'Ethics for AI-assisted and digital-trace research', 'Assess consent, privacy, provenance, data quality, bias, human oversight and disclosure when research uses AI systems or traces left by online activity.', 'Assess human oversight, data quality, provenance, consent, privacy, bias and disclosure when AI or online traces are used.', 'An ethics and governance note that identifies the data source, permissions, risks, human checks, disclosure plan and limits on reuse or interpretation.', 'build_next', 'Assess human oversight, data quality, provenance, consent, privacy, bias and disclosure when AI or online traces are used. Keep AI as a conditional method/data-use extension, not an occupation, replacement for participants, or general research requirement. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['esrc_research_ethics_core_principles_2026', 'esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022', 'nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum', 'aapor_responsible_ai_explanation_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"esrc_research_ethics_core_principles_2026","title":"Framework for research ethics: core principles","url":"https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/framework-for-research-ethics/our-core-principles/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"esrc_social_science_training_guidelines_2022","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines 2022","url":"https://www.ukri.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/ESRC-281123-PostgraduateTrainingDevelopmentGuidelines2022.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nuc_social_sciences_ccmas_2023_research_curriculum","title":"Social Sciences CCMAS 2023: research-methods curriculum examples","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng