('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'method', 'd078_statsmodels', 'statsmodels', 'statsmodels is a Python library for fitting and inspecting selected statistical models, including regression and time-series models. It provides calculations and diagnostics; it does not decide whether the model answers the social question or whether causal claims are justified.', 'Fit and inspect regression, generalised linear, mixed-effects, time-series and related statistical models.', 'Model estimates, diagnostics and reproducible code with assumptions and qualified substantive interpretation.', 'useful_later', 'Fit and inspect regression, generalised linear, mixed-effects, time-series and related statistical models. The package cannot select a defensible model, correct poor measurement or establish causality/fairness by itself. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['url_8e2a358e49228989', 'statsmodels_official_user_guide_2026']::text[], '[{"id":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"statsmodels_official_user_guide_2026","title":"Study statsmodels model and time-series examples","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/user-guide.html","region":"global","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","locator":"Raw-data workflow: specify a model, fit it, inspect results and diagnostics; pandas and patsy dependencies","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","locator":"The example explicitly separates substantive motivation, model design, fitting and diagnostics","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","locator":"Case study from raw data through model specification, fitting, summary and diagnostics","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["It cannot decide whether a model is justified or whether its assumptions hold.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/user-guide.html', 'Study statsmodels model and time-series examples', '{"source_id":"statsmodels_official_user_guide_2026","title":"Study statsmodels model and time-series examples","publisher":null,"url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/user-guide.html","locator":"User Guide sections for regression, statistical models, time-series analysis, diagnostics and worked examples","accessed_on":"2026-10-09","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-09', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/user-guide.html","locator":"User Guide sections for regression, statistical models, time-series analysis, diagnostics and worked examples","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":"Free online documentation and examples"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"url_8e2a358e49228989","title":"statsmodels getting started","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/gettingstarted.html","locator":"Raw-data workflow: specify a model, fit it, inspect results and diagnostics; pandas and patsy dependencies","claimRole":"item_ident