('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078_scikit_learn', 'scikit-learn', 'scikit-learn is a Python library for selected machine-learning workflows such as classification, prediction, clustering and text-feature processing. It helps implement a model; it cannot decide whether the social concept, labels, sample or interpretation are sound.', 'Predictive and text-feature modelling when a clearly defined research question, evaluation plan and bias/interpretation safeguards exist.', 'A documented, repeatable text- or table-analysis pipeline: the research question and labels; how data were prepared; model and feature choices; held-out evaluation (for classification, for example, precision/recall and a confusion matrix); error checks; and a statement of what the model can and cannot support.', 'useful_later', 'Predictive and text-feature modelling when a clearly defined research question, evaluation plan and bias/interpretation safeguards exist. Prediction does not establish explanation, causality, fairness or social validity; assess leakage, bias, baselines and limits. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['sklearn_feature_extraction_user_guide_2026', 'sklearn_mooc_text_dimensionality_2026', 'url_d9a6758138024a39', 'sicss_nigeria_uyo_2026_computational_social_science', 'uw_text_as_data_social_science_workshop', 'nigerian_pidgin_contextual_sentiment_2020', 'uw_text_as_data_social_science_explanation', 'url_27374328743a0995']::text[], '[{"id":"sklearn_feature_extraction_user_guide_2026","title":"Feature extraction — scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/feature_extraction.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"sklearn_mooc_text_dimensionality_2026","title":"Dimensionality reduction of text data — scikit-learn MOOC","url":"https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"sicss_nigeria_uyo_2026_computational_social_science","title":"Summer Institute in Computational Social Science: Nigeria 2026","url":"https://new.sicss.io/2026/uyo/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_workshop","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"nigerian_pidgin_contextual_sentiment_2020","title":"Semantic Enrichment of Nigerian Pidgin English for Contextual Sentiment Classification","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.12450","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_explanation","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_27374328743a0995","title":"University of Washington: Introduction to Text as Data","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"sklearn_feature_extraction_user_guide_2026","title":"Feature extraction — scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/feature_extraction.html","locator":"Sections 8.2 and 8.2.3.7–8.2.3.8: turning text into numerical features; text classification/clustering examples; and bag-of-words limitations, including loss of word order and multi-word structure.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"sklearn_mooc_text_dimensionality_2026","title":"Dimensionality reduction of text data — scikit-learn MOOC","url":"https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html","locator":"The notebook uses TfidfVectorizer on a text corpus, explains the resulting document-term feature space and explores dimensionality reduction; the adjacent course overview describes the free, openly licensed, executable MOOC.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","locator":"Supervised learning, model evaluation, text feature extraction and preprocessing sections","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"sicss_nigeria_uyo_2026_computational_social_science","title":"Summer Institute in Computational Social Science: Nigeria 2026","url":"https://new.sicss.io/2026/uyo/","locator":"Programme description lists NLP for social research, dataset preprocessing, feature engineering, machine learning for social insight, and classification/clustering; audience and event dates are stated on the page.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_workshop","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","locator":"Workshop description and materials: selecting and representing text, building measures from unstructured text, social-science/demography applications, Python demos and Colab; the page says no prior text-data experience is required and some Python is helpful.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","locator":"Supervised learning, model evaluation and text-feature extraction; technical capability does not establish social-science validity","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"nigerian_pidgin_contextual_sentiment_2020","title":"Semantic Enrichment of Nigerian Pidgin English for Contextual Sentiment Classification","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.12450","locator":"Abstract and sections 2–4: the study describes contextual differences in Nigerian Pidgin/code-mixed terms, its sentiment dataset and human-speaker checking; the method uses VADER rather than scikit-learn.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_explanation","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","locator":"Workshop overview, lines 64–75: explains representing text and building measures for social-science/demography questions; Python and tutorial links are included.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"url_27374328743a0995","title":"University of Washington: Introduction to Text as Data","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","locator":"Social-science questions, text representation and human interpretation alongside Python demonstrations","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A model learns patterns in the examples and labels it receives; it does not decide whether a social concept was measured well, a label is fair, or a result is meaningful.","Good held-out prediction does not establish causality, representativeness, construct validity, fairness or the truth of an interpretation; the study design and evidence still govern those claims.","Bag-of-words text features can discard word order and multi-word meaning. The official guide notes that this loses much of a document''s internal structure.","English-only text features may miss local meanings in Nigerian Pidgin or code-mixed text. A 2020 Nigerian Pidgin sentiment study found that direct English sentiment analysis missed contextual meanings in its dataset; this is a bounded example, not a finding about every Nigerian language or task.","This candidate is conditional specialist software, not a shared D078 foundation, a required library for every route, a professional credential, or evidence that a learner can independently conduct valid research.","Prediction alone does not establish explanation, causality, fairness or social validity.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html', 'Learn scikit-learn text features with a hands-on notebook', '{"source_id":"sklearn_mooc_text_dimensionality_2026","title":"Learn scikit-learn text features with a hands-on notebook","publisher":null,"url":"https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html","locator":"Dimensionality reduction of text data: TfidfVectorizer, document-term features and text dimensionality reduction. Use the MOOC page''s Binder/rocket control to run notebook cells where available.","accessed_on":"2026-10-09","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-09', 'medium', '{"url":"https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html","locator":"Dimensionality reduction of text data: TfidfVectorizer, document-term features and text dimensionality reduction. Use the MOOC page''s Binder/rocket control to run notebook cells where available.","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":"Free online MOOC material, openly licensed CC BY; interactive notebooks can be launched with Binder; some online quiz features may require the course platform."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"sklearn_feature_extraction_user_guide_2026","title":"Feature extraction — scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/feature_extraction.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"sklearn_mooc_text_dimensionality_2026","title":"Dimensionality reduction of text data — scikit-learn MOOC","url":"https://inria.github.io/scikit-learn-mooc/python_scripts/dimred_text.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","region":null,"evidenceType":