s://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","locator":"Workshop description and materials: selecting and representing text, building measures from unstructured text, social-science/demography applications, Python demos and Colab; the page says no prior text-data experience is required and some Python is helpful.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","locator":"Supervised learning, model evaluation and text-feature extraction; technical capability does not establish social-science validity","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]},"expected_output":{"source_references":[{"id":"sicss_nigeria_uyo_2026_computational_social_science","title":"Summer Institute in Computational Social Science: Nigeria 2026","url":"https://new.sicss.io/2026/uyo/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_workshop","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"sicss_nigeria_uyo_2026_computational_social_science","title":"Summer Institute in Computational Social Science: Nigeria 2026","url":"https://new.sicss.io/2026/uyo/","locator":"Programme description lists NLP for social research, dataset preprocessing, feature engineering, machine learning for social insight, and classification/clustering; audience and event dates are stated on the page.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"uw_text_as_data_social_science_workshop","title":"Text as Data and LLM Applications","url":"https://csde.washington.edu/workshop/introduction-to-text-as-data/","locator":"Workshop description and materials: selecting and representing text, building measures from unstructured text, social-science/demography applications, Python demos and Colab; the page says no prior text-data experience is required and some Python is helpful.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"url_d9a6758138024a39","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html","locator":"Supervised learning, model evaluation and text-feature extraction; technical capability does not establish social-science validity","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"d078_scikit_learn"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', 'Introductory-to-intermediate; basic Python is expected', 'English', 'Free online MOOC material, openly licensed CC BY; interactive notebooks can be launched with Binder; some online quiz features may require the course platform.', NULL, 'specialist_predictive_and_text_modelling_library', 'Specialist predictive and text modelling library', 'specialist_predictive_and_text_modelling_library', 'optional', 'Predictive and text-feature modelling when a clearly defined research question, evaluation plan and bias/interpretation safeguards exist. Prediction does not establish explanation, causality, fairness or social validity; assess leakage, bias, baselines and limits. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.'),
('domain', 'D078', 'D078', 'tool', 'd078-jamovi-tool', 'jamovi for introductory quantitative social-science analysis', 'jamovi is a free statistical application with a spreadsheet-like interface. A learner can enter or import a dataset, organise variables, run selected descriptive or inferential analyses, and inspect tables or plots. It can make some analysis steps more accessible, but it does not choose a valid research design, repair poor measurement, or interpret results on the learner''s behalf.', 'Use it when a selected social-science task needs introductory numerical summaries or a supported statistical test and a graphical workflow is suitable. Examples include summarising a small survey dataset, inspecting a relationship with a scatterplot, or carrying out a justified correlation or t-test. The method and assumptions must be chosen before clicking an analysis menu.', 'A documented analysis file or exported table/plot, with variable definitions, missing-data decisions, the selected method, an interpretation in relation to the research question, and limits on what the result can establish.', 'build_next', 'Use it when a selected social-science task needs introductory numerical summaries or a supported statistical test and a graphical workflow is suitable. Examples include summarising a small survey dataset, inspecting a relationship with a scatterplot, or carrying out a justified correlation or t-test. The method and assumptions must be chosen before clicking an analysis menu. Does not replace quantitative-method knowledge, research design, measurement, data ethics or interpretation; no role requirement is inferred. Optional domain-enrichment choice for the named task only; not required for every D078 learner or occupation, not proof of competence, and not claimed to be taught by the Sociology programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['url_f0445d8520395bda', 'url_db34b999eab97946', 'url_78023be73e60aa29']::text[], '[{"id":"url_f0445d8520395bda","title":"Getting started — jamovi documentation","url":"https://docs.jamovi.org/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_db34b999eab97946","title":"Getting started with Jamovi","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"url_78023be73e60aa29","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines","url":"https://www.ukri.org/publications/esrc-postgraduate-training-and-development-guidelines/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"url_f0445d8520395bda","title":"Getting started — jamovi documentation","url":"https://docs.jamovi.org/","locator":"Official documentation overview and links to analyses, data and R integration","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"url_db34b999eab97946","title":"Getting started with Jamovi","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","locator":"OpenLearn describes introductory statistics for social-science learners and gives task examples; this supports optional quantitative-route use, not universal D078 requirement","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"url_78023be73e60aa29","title":"ESRC Postgraduate Training and Development Guidelines","url":"https://www.ukri.org/publications/esrc-postgraduate-training-and-development-guidelines/","locator":"Annex II, printed p. 8; quantitative methods are specialist and discipline-/project-dependent","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"url_db34b999eab97946","title":"Getting started with Jamovi — Introduction","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","locator":"Introductory course explains the tool and the statistical ideas alongside social-science examples","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["This is an optional tool for selected quantitative tasks, not a shared foundation requirement across all D078 routes.","A menu can calculate a test but cannot decide whether the question, sample, measures, assumptions or comparison justify it.","A p-value or chart does not by itself establish causation, representativeness, practical importance or policy impact.","The linked course is introductory and does not cover every statistical method, discipline-specific design or advanced analysis.","Domain enrichment only. The programme-to-domain relationship does not mean this item is taught by the Sociology degree."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1', 'Start the free Jamovi course for introductory social-science statistics', '{"source_id":"openlearn_jamovi","title":"Start the free Jamovi course for introductory social-science statistics","publisher":null,"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","locator":"Course activities on navigation, variables, descriptive statistics, correlation, scatterplots and t-tests","accessed_on":"2026-10-10","scope_limit":null}'::jsonb, '2026-10-10', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/getting-started-jamovi/content-section-0?intro=1","locator":"Course activities on navigation, variables, descriptive statistics, correlation, scatterplots and t-tests","supports":"Task-specific learning resource for the item","access":"Free OpenLearn course; course pages can be opened without enrolment; account supports progress and statement of participation"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'domain', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"url_f0445d8520395bda","title":"Getting started — jamovi documentation","url":"https://docs.jamovi.org/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"url_f0445d8520395bda","title":"Getting started — jamovi documentation","url":"ht