ence:data-provenance-and-digital-ethics"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Described as free, interactive, self-paced modules; requires web access.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'computational-digital-social-science', 'useful', 'Apply permissions, provenance, privacy and risk checks to the selected digital data; UK guidance is not Nigerian legal advice.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:reproducible-data-cleaning', 'Clean and document a social-science dataset reproducibly', 'The skill of importing, checking, transforming and documenting data so another person can understand and rerun the work.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Use for a computational data workflow; retain documentation and protect sensitive information rather than sharing raw data by default.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Use for a computational data workflow; retain documentation and protect sensitive information rather than sharing raw data by default.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_DOC_SOCSCI', 'PANDAS_TUTORIALS', 'PYTHON_SOCSCI']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_DOC_SOCSCI","title":"Best practices for documenting social sciences research data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/app/uploads/documentingsocialsciences2024-11-26.pdf","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"PANDAS_TUTORIALS","title":"Getting started tutorials","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/getting_started/intro_tutorials/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"PYTHON_SOCSCI","title":"Data Analysis and Visualization with Python for Social Scientists (alpha)","url":"https://datacarpentry.org/python-socialsci/","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_DOC_SOCSCI","title":"Best practices for documenting social sciences research data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/app/uploads/documentingsocialsciences2024-11-26.pdf","locator":"Guide sections on documenting social-science data, metadata and decisions for reuse.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"PANDAS_TUTORIALS","t