('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'method', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:interpretable-statistical-modeling', 'Interpretable statistical modelling when the question and design justify it', 'A statistical modelling route that uses a stated design, assumptions, uncertainty and interpretation rather than treating software output as an answer.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Optional quantitative route; requires suitable design, assumptions, diagnostics and interpretation, not code alone.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional quantitative route; requires suitable design, assumptions, diagnostics and interpretation, not code alone.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['STATSMODELS_DIAGNOSTICS', 'MIT_DA_SOCSCI']::text[], '[{"id":"STATSMODELS_DIAGNOSTICS","title":"Linear regression diagnostics; Regression diagnostics","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/examples/notebooks/generated/linear_regression_diagnostics_plots.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"MIT_DA_SOCSCI","title":"Data Analysis for Social Scientists (14.310x, Spring 2023)","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/14-310x-data-analysis-for-social-scientists-spring-2023/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"STATSMODELS_DIAGNOSTICS","title":"Linear regression diagnostics; Regression diagnostics","url":"https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/examples/notebooks/generated/linear_regression_diagnostics_plots.html","locator":"Runnable example with OLS output, residual/QQ/scale-location/leverage diagnostics, VIF and discussion of failure modes; companion regression diagnostics notebook.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MIT_DA_SOCSCI","title":"Data Analysis for Social Scientists (14.310x, Spring 2023)","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/14-310x-data-analysis-for-social-scientists-spring-2023/","locator":"Course description and available lecture/assignment materials on statistics, regression/econometrics, experiments, R and empirical social-science analysis.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MIT_DA_SOCSCI","title":"Data Analysis for Social Scientists (14.310x, Spring 2023)","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/14-310x-data-analysis-for-social-scientists-spring-2023/","locator":"Lecture notes, problem sets and course materials for probability/statistics, regression/econometrics, research design and applied social-science analysis.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A fitted model is not causal proof; assumptions and omitted variables matter.","Technical model accuracy may not equal substantive validity or policy usefulness.","Optional quantitative route; requires suitable design, assumptions, diagnostics and interpretation, not code alone."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/14-310x-data-analysis-for-social-scientists-spring-2023/', 'Data Analysis for Social Scientists (14.310x, Spring 2023)', '{"source_id":"MIT_DA_SOCSCI","title":"Data Analysis for Social Scientists (14.310x, Spring 2023)","publisher":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/14-310x-data-analysis-for-social-scientists-spring-2023/","locator":"Lecture notes, problem sets and course materials for probability/statistics, regression/econometrics, research design and applied social-science analysis.","what_supported":"Free structured social-science analysis learning that contextualizes models in questions, designs and evidence.","limitations":"Requires substantial math/statistics preparation; materials are from a 2023 course and examples are not locally tailored.","cost_access":"Materials free; no charge for self-study. No graded certificate or