('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:digital-trace-construct-and-sampling', 'Define the construct, platform scope and sampling limits of digital traces', 'Knowledge of how digital traces are generated, what population/platform they cover, and how collection and sampling decisions affect interpretation.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Define the construct, platform, population and sampling before interpreting traces; online activity is not automatically representative.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Define the construct, platform, population and sampling before interpreting traces; online activity is not automatically representative.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UTRECHT_DIGITAL_TRACE', 'SICSS_DIGITAL_TRACE']::text[], '[{"id":"UTRECHT_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Introduction to digital trace data: Quality, ethics, and analysis","url":"https://digitaltracedata.github.io/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Learning Materials: Collecting Digital Trace Data","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UTRECHT_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Introduction to digital trace data: Quality, ethics, and analysis","url":"https://digitaltracedata.github.io/","locator":"Course overview and 2026/27 schedule; course focus on how behavioral data are collected, analysed and interpreted, with quality, ethics and inequality; linked lectures, labs and solutions.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SICSS_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Learning Materials: Collecting Digital Trace Data","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Day 2: Collecting Digital Trace Data and linked lectures, slides, code and exercises.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SICSS_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Learning Materials: Collecting Digital Trace Data","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Day 2: Collecting Digital Trace Data; linked lecture, slides, code and exercises.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Platform users may not represent the public; model output does not show prevalence, causation or human meaning automatically.","Terms-of-service and privacy issues vary.","Define the construct, platform, population and sampling before interpreting traces; online activity is not automatically representative."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://sicss.io/curriculum', 'Learning Materials: Collecting Digital Trace Data', '{"source_id":"SICSS_DIGITAL_TRACE","title":"Learning Materials: Collecting Digital Trace Data","publisher":"Summer Institutes in Computational Social Science","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Day 2: Collecting Digital Trace Data; linked lecture, slides, code and exercises.","what_supported":"Free structured instruction to examine digital-trace collection choices as a research task.","limitations":"Requires basic R for much of the curriculum; learners must separately establish construct validity, platform terms, ethical permission and sampling limits for their own case.","cost_access":"Materials are open source/free; no course fee for self-study of materials. Data/API access may have separate costs or restrictions.","accessed_on":"2026-10-12"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Day 2: Collecting Digital Trace Data; linked lecture, slides, code and exercises.","supports":"Free structured instruction to examine digital-trace collection choices as a research task.","access":"Materials are open source/free; no course fee for self-study of materials. Data/API access may have separate costs or restrictions."}':