('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'method', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:agent-based-social-simulation', 'Agent-based modelling for a stated social mechanism', 'A method for representing agents, states, rules and interactions to explore scenarios and possible emergent patterns under explicit assumptions.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Specialist simulation option for a stated mechanism; simulated agents and outcomes are not observations about real people.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Specialist simulation option for a stated mechanism; simulated agents and outcomes are not observations about real people.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['MESA_FIRST_MODEL', 'SICSS_SIMULATION']::text[], '[{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"First-model notebook progressively implements agents, model steps, data collection and visualisation; model assumptions are listed explicitly.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Course curriculum links lectures, slides, code and exercises in computational social science, including method and ethics foundations.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Step-by-step Boltzmann wealth model notebook; introduces agent/model structure, steps and adding data collection and visualization.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Simulated outcomes depend on rules and parameters; they do not establish real-world prevalence, causal truth or prediction accuracy.","A visually impressive simulation is not validation.","Specialist simulation option for a stated mechanism; simulated agents and outcomes are not observations about real people."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html', 'Creating Your First Model', '{"source_id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model","publisher":"Mesa project","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Step-by-step Boltzmann wealth model notebook; introduces agent/model structure, steps and adding data collection and visualization.","what_supported":"Free hands-on ABM implementation lesson with explicit model rules and recorded outputs.","limitations":"A simple illustrative model only; learner must justify mechanism, inspect sensitivity and compare with relevant empirical evidence before drawing claims.","cost_access":"Free documentation and open-source framework; local Python setup or free third-party hosted notebook may be used. Hosted uptime is not guaranteed.","accessed_on":"2026-10-12"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Step-by-step Boltzmann wealth model notebook; introduces agent/model structure, steps and adding data collection and visualization.","supports":"Free hands-on ABM implementation lesson with explicit model rules and recorded outputs.","access":"Free documentation and open-source framework; local Python setup or free third-party hosted notebook may be used. Hosted uptime is not guaranteed."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"First-model notebook progressively implements agents, model steps, data collection and visualisation; model assumptions are listed explicitly.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Course curriculum links lectures, slides, code and exercises in computational social science, including method and ethics foundations.","claimRole":"item_identity"}]},"checkpoint_fit":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"First-model notebook progressively implements agents, model steps, data collection and visualisation; model assumptions are listed explicitly.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Course curriculum links lectures, slides, code and exercises in computational social science, including method and ethics foundations.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"First-model notebook progressively implements agents, model steps, data collection and visualisation; model assumptions are listed explicitly.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Course curriculum links lectures, slides, code and exercises in computational social science, including method and ethics foundations.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model: The Boltzmann Wealth Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"First-model notebook progressively implements agents, model steps, data collection and visualisation; model assumptions are listed explicitly.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"SICSS_SIMULATION","title":"Computational Social Science learning materials","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Course curriculum links lectures, slides, code and exercises in computational social science, including method and ethics foundations.","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078:computational-digital-social-science:agent-based-social-simulation"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free documentation and open-source framework; local Python setup or free third-party hosted notebook may be used. Hosted uptime is not guaranteed.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'computational-digital-social-science', 'useful', 'Specialist simulation option for a stated mechanism; simulated agents and outcomes are not observations about real people.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:mesa-or-casevo', 'Mesa for social simulation (Casevo not established)', 'Mesa is a general Python agent-based-modelling framework; Casevo is a narrower emerging cognitive-agent/social-evolution project.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Mesa has a free runnable learning route. Casevo is an optional experimental branch requiring a Baichuan API account and paid usage; availability, cost and model compatibility must be checked before use. Do not silently require Casevo.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Mesa has a free runnable learning route. Casevo is an optional experimental branch requiring a Baichuan API account and paid usage; availability, cost and model compatibility must be checked before use. Do not silently require Casevo.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS', 'CASEVO_REPOSITORY', 'MESA_FIRST_MODEL']::text[], '[{"id":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","locator":"Framework overview and linked tutorials for first model, agent activation, scheduling, space, data collection and visualization.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README: introduction, installation, basic tutorial and election-debate simulation; example implementation calls a separately configured Baichuan LLM API.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Beginner notebook builds an agent model step by step; companion Getting Started page links scheduling, data collection and visualization tutorials.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Neither framework proves the model describes real people; Casevo is emerging and narrow.","Framework completion or generated agent output is not certification.","An official Casevo tutorial and an official paid Baichuan API path are now documented. A free end-to-end Casevo run remains unverified; account availability from Nigeria, current model compatibility, pinned reproducibility and teaching-level maintenance still require a hands-on check. Keep Casevo optional with cost/availability disclosure; Mesa is the documented free runnable alternative.","Mesa has a free runnable learning route. Casevo is an optional experimental branch requiring a Baichuan API account and paid usage; availability, cost and model compatibility must be checked before use. Do not silently require Casevo."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html', 'Creating Your First Model', '{"source_id":"MESA_FIRST_MODEL","title":"Creating Your First Model","publisher":"Mesa project","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Beginner notebook builds an agent model step by step; companion Getting Started page links scheduling, data collection and visualization tutorials.","what_supported":"Free runnable social-simulation framework instruction, suitable for the Mesa branch of this alternative-platform item.","limitations":"The example is a toy model, not an empirical claim or a validated account of human behavior. Does not teach Casevo or establish Casevo''s API costs/maintenance as solved.","cost_access":"Free/open-source Mesa materials; Python environment and computer required. Cloud notebook option may have limits.","accessed_on":"2026-10-12"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/tutorials/0_first_model.html","locator":"Beginner notebook builds an agent model step by step; companion Getting Started page links scheduling, data collection and visualization tutorials.","supports":"Free runnable social-simulation framework instruction, suitable for the Mesa branch of this alternative-platform item.","access":"Free/open-source Mesa materials; Python environment and computer required. Cloud notebook option may have limits."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","locator":"Framework overview and linked tutorials for first model, agent activation, scheduling, space, data collection and visualization.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README: introduction, installation, basic tutorial and election-debate simulation; example implementation calls a separately configured Baichuan LLM API.","claimRole":"item_identity"}]},"checkpoint_fit":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","locator":"Framework overview and linked tutorials for first model, agent activation, scheduling, space, data collection and visualization.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README: introduction, installation, basic tutorial and election-debate simulation; example implementation calls a separately configured Baichuan LLM API.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","locator":"Framework overview and linked tutorials for first model, agent activation, scheduling, space, data collection and visualization.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README: introduction, installation, basic tutorial and election-debate simulation; example implementation calls a separately configured Baichuan LLM API.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MESA_GETTING_STARTED_READTHEDOCS","title":"Getting started","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/getting_started.html","locator":"Framework overview and linked tutorials for first model, agent activation, scheduling, space, data collection and visualization.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README: introduction, installation, basic tutorial and election-debate simulation; example implementation calls a separately configured Baichuan LLM API.","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078:computational-digital-social-science:mesa-or-casevo"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free/open-source Mesa materials; Python environment and computer required. Cloud notebook option may have limits.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'computational-digital-social-science', 'optional', 'Mesa has a free runnable learning route. Casevo is an optional experimental branch requiring a Baichuan API account and paid usage; availability, cost and model compatibility must be checked before use. Do not silently require Casevo.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078:computational-digital-social-science:predictive-text-modeling', 'Predictive/text modelling only after social validation safeguards', 'A later computational option for feature extraction, supervised prediction or text classification when the construct, labelled data, evaluation and harm/ethics plan are explicit.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Show the bounded AfriSenti sentiment-classification practice route (Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yoruba) only. This does not validate other constructs, populations or general Nigerian social prediction; learners must check lawful access, labels, language coverage and subgroup errors.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Show the bounded AfriSenti sentiment-classification practice route (Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yoruba) only. This does not validate other constructs, populations or general Nigerian social prediction; learners must check lawful access, labels, language coverage and subgroup errors.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL', 'SICSS_TEXT', 'AFRISENTI_SEMEVAL_TASK_PAPER']::text[], '[{"id":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_TEXT","title":"Learning Materials: Text as Data and computational social science","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AFRISENTI_SEMEVAL_TASK_PAPER","title":"SemEval-2023 Task 12: Sentiment Analysis for African Languages (AfriSenti-SemEval)","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","locator":"Tutorial steps: load text data, extract features, train a classifier, build a pipeline and evaluate performance.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SICSS_TEXT","title":"Learning Materials: Text as Data and computational social science","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Curriculum links for text analysis, computational social-science methods and ethics.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AFRISENTI_SEMEVAL_TASK_PAPER","title":"SemEval-2023 Task 12: Sentiment Analysis for African Languages (AfriSenti-SemEval)","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315/","locator":"Task definition, language list, data/annotation overview and evaluation results; includes Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yorùbá. Official task presentation video: https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315.mp4. Dataset repository: https://github.com/afrisenti-semeval/afrisent-semeval-2023.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","locator":"Hands-on pipeline from loading labeled text through feature extraction, classifier training and performance evaluation; linked 20 Newsgroups example.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Accuracy or AUC does not prove construct validity, causation, fairness or generalisation.","Platform and language bias can be severe; no automatic Nigerian transfer.","A practical route now exists for sentiment classification using AfriSenti material that includes Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yorùbá, alongside an official task video and implementation lessons. This does not resolve validation for an unspecified target construct/population. AfriSenti''s sentiment labels cannot validate wellbeing, political attitudes or other constructs; for any chosen study, define the construct/population, confirm lawful data use, obtain suitable reference labels, check language/dialect coverage and report subgroup errors before making claims. Keep only the bounded sentiment exercise in scope; do not present generalized Nigerian social prediction as validated.","Show the bounded AfriSenti sentiment-classification practice route (Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yoruba) only. This does not validate other constructs, populations or general Nigerian social prediction; learners must check lawful access, labels, language coverage and subgroup errors."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html', 'Working with text data', '{"source_id":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","publisher":"scikit-learn project","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","locator":"Hands-on pipeline from loading labeled text through feature extraction, classifier training and performance evaluation; linked 20 Newsgroups example.","what_supported":"Free practical text-classification implementation instruction with an evaluation step.","limitations":"The example is English-language news text, not Nigerian social research; it does not teach construct validity, lawful access, representativeness, subgroup harms or cross-language validation. It cannot close those evidence gaps.","cost_access":"Free/open-source docs, library and example dataset access; local compute and internet required.","accessed_on":"2026-10-12"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","locator":"Hands-on pipeline from loading labeled text through feature extraction, classifier training and performance evaluation; linked 20 Newsgroups example.","supports":"Free practical text-classification implementation instruction with an evaluation step.","access":"Free/open-source docs, library and example dataset access; local compute and internet required."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_TEXT","title":"Learning Materials: Text as Data and computational social science","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AFRISENTI_SEMEVAL_TASK_PAPER","title":"SemEval-2023 Task 12: Sentiment Analysis for African Languages (AfriSenti-SemEval)","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"SKLEARN_TEXT_TUTORIAL","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/text_analytics/working_with_text_data.html","locator":"Tutorial steps: load text data, extract features, train a classifier, build a pipeline and evaluate performance.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"SICSS_TEXT","title":"Learning Materials: Text as Data and computational social science","url":"https://sicss.io/curriculum","locator":"Curriculum links for text analysis, computational social-science methods and ethics.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"AFRISENTI_SEMEVAL_TASK_PAPER","title":"SemEval-2023 Task 12: Sentiment Analysis for African Languages (AfriSenti-SemEval)","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315/","locator":"Task definition, language list, data/annotation overview and evaluation results; includes Hausa, Igbo, Nigerian Pidgin and Yorùbá. Official task presentation video: https://aclanthology.org/2023.semeval-1.315.mp4. Dataset repository: https://github.com/afrisenti-semeval/afrisent-semeval-2023.","claimRole":"item_identity"}]},"checkpoint_fit":{"source_references":[{"id":"SKLEARN_