('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078-ECON-MEASUREMENT', 'Economic measurement and source/data appraisal', 'Understanding how economic quantities and indicators are defined, constructed, sampled, weighted, revised, and limited.', 'Economic analysis depends on measurement choices such as nominal versus real values, per-capita rates, price indices, or labour definitions; this knowledge is an economics-specific elaboration, not just generic data handling. Check units, period, population, price basis, definitions, coverage, weighting, and revisions; produce a data note that makes a chart or estimate interpretable. Not claimed as taught by a selected programme absent direct curriculum evidence. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Check units, period, population, price basis, definitions, coverage, weighting, and revisions; produce a data note that makes a chart or estimate interpretable. Guardrail: GDP, CPI, employment, and other indicators each capture limited constructs. Data revisions and methodology changes can break na�ve time-series comparisons.', 'Check units, period, population, price basis, definitions, coverage, weighting, and revisions; produce a data note that makes a chart or estimate interpretable.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Check units, period, population, price basis, definitions, coverage, weighting, and revisions; produce a data note that makes a chart or estimate interpretable. Guardrail: GDP, CPI, employment, and other indicators each capture limited constructs. Data revisions and methodology changes can break na�ve time-series comparisons.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ONET_ECONOMIST', 'NBS_CATALOG', 'NBS_NLFS', 'CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS']::text[], '[{"id":"ONET_ECONOMIST","title":"Economi