('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078-ECON-UNCERTAINTY-COMMUNICATION', 'Economic interpretation and uncertainty communication', 'The ability to explain what an economic table, model, estimate, forecast, or recommendation means in plain language, including uncertainty and limits.', 'Economic findings often inform decisions; audiences need to know whether a result is descriptive, predictive, or causal and how robust it is. Prepare a concise brief or chart note that separates observation, estimate, interpretation, assumption, and recommendation and avoids stronger claims than the evidence supports. Communication is an area task, but no course-specific achievement is inferred. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Prepare a concise brief or chart note that separates observation, estimate, interpretation, assumption, and recommendation and avoids stronger claims than the evidence supports. Guardrail: A polished chart cannot repair invalid measurement or design. Recommendations also involve values, feasibility, and distributional choices.', 'Prepare a concise brief or chart note that separates observation, estimate, interpretation, assumption, and recommendation and avoids stronger claims than the evidence supports.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Prepare a concise brief or chart note that separates observation, estimate, interpretation, assumption, and recommendation and avoids stronger claims than the evidence supports. Guardrail: A polished chart cannot repair invalid measurement or design. Recommendations also involve values, feasibility, and distributional choices.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ONET_ECONOMIST', 'WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION']::text[], '[{"id":"ONET_ECONOMIST","title":"Economists, 19-3011.00","url":"https