ory mastery checkpoint. Task: Prepare a concise brief or chart note that separates observation, estimate, interpretation, assumption, and recommendation and avoids stronger claims than the evidence supports. Guardrail: A polished chart cannot repair invalid measurement or design. Recommendations also involve values, feasibility, and distributional choices.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-ECON-APPLIED-ECONOMETRICS', 'Applied econometric analysis with assumptions and diagnostics', 'Statistical methods used to estimate and assess economic relationships using observed data.', 'Econometrics adds economic interpretation and identification questions to general statistics; not all economic questions require regression or advanced econometrics. Not asserted as curriculum-taught without specific evidence. Route note: Optional applied-economics method for estimating and checking economic relationships with observed data. Introduce only for a relevant economic question; regression alone does not establish causality. The linked CORE Econ material is a worked-data learning route, not a complete econometrics qualification.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional applied-economics method for estimating and checking economic relationships with observed data. Introduce only for a relevant economic question; regression alone does not establish causality. The linked CORE Econ material is a worked-data learning route, not a complete econometrics qualification.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS', 'ONET_ECONOMIST', 'CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS', 'WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION', 'CORE_R_EXPERIMENT']::text[], '[{"id":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","region":"International economics research; examples/method debate not a universal protocol","evidenceType":null},{"id":"ONET_ECONOMIST","title":"Economists, 19-3011.00","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link/details/19-3011.00","region":"United States","evidenceType":null},{"id":"CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS","title":"Doing Economics","url":"https://www.core-econ.org/project/doing-economics/","region":"Global open educational resource","evidenceType":null},{"id":"WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION","title":"Impact Evaluation in Practice, 2nd edition","u