nd readxl packages","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Regression association does not by itself establish causality.","Bad measurement, selection, omitted variables, or misspecification can invalidate interpretation.","Optional applied-economics method for estimating and checking economic relationships with observed data. Introduce only for a relevant economic question; regression alone does not establish causality. The linked CORE Econ material is a worked-data learning route, not a complete econometrics qualification."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://books.core-econ.org/doing-economics/book/text/02-03.html', 'Collecting and analysing data from experiments – Working in R', '{"source_id":"CORE_R_EXPERIMENT","publisher":"CORE Econ","title":"Collecting and analysing data from experiments – Working in R","url":"https://books.core-econ.org/doing-economics/book/text/02-03.html","locator":"Learning objectives and worked R workflow for experimental economic data; names tidyverse and readxl packages","jurisdiction":"Global open educational resource","evidence_use":"Exact free learning link for R economic data analysis; one task workflow.","accessed":"2026-10-10"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-10', 'medium', '{"url":"https://books.core-econ.org/doing-economics/book/text/02-03.html","locator":"Learning objectives and worked R workflow for experimental economic data; names tidyverse and readxl packages","supports":null,"access":null}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","region":"International economics research; examples/method debate not a universal protocol","evidenceType":null},{"id":"ONET_ECONOMIST","title":"Economists, 19-3011.00","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link