('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-ECON-R-PYTHON-ANALYSIS', 'Reproducible economic data analysis (R or Python; select a workflow)', 'R and Python are programming environments used to import, clean, analyze, visualize, and document economic data; they are alternatives for many workflows, not two compulsory languages.', 'Economics-specific practice connects code to measured concepts and methods. R is widely supported in open teaching materials such as CORE; Python is also supported by project notebooks. Choose based on task, team, and learning route. Use a notebook or script to reproduce a data transformation, summary, estimate, or chart from source files and record package versions and decisions. No programme-provision claim; this is additional tool learning. Route note: Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Use a notebook or script to reproduce a data transformation, summary, estimate, or chart from source files and record package versions and decisions. Guardrail: Do not require learners to master both R and Python for the same task. Packages do not establish construct validity, causal identification, or economic interpretation.', 'Use a notebook or script to reproduce a data transformation, summary, estimate, or chart from source files and record package versions and decisions.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Use a notebook or script to reproduce a data transformation, summary, estimate, or chart from source files and record package versions and decisions. Guardrail: Do not require learners to master both R and Python for the same task. Packages do not establish construct validity, causal identification, or economic interpretation.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS', 'CORE_R_EXPERIMENT', 'CORE_PYTHON_WELLBEING', 'WB_REPRODUCIBLE']::text