('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-ECON-CAUSAL-ML', 'Machine learning for causal questions (double/debiased ML or heterogeneous effects when justified)', 'Methods that use flexible prediction tools to help estimate causal effects under specific identification frameworks, such as high-dimensional adjustment or variation in treatment effects.', 'A specialist extension for economic empirical research with rich covariates or heterogeneous effects, not a general-purpose replacement for econometrics or causal design. Advanced useful edge; not assumed taught at undergraduate programme level. Route note: Advanced optional route for causal-effect questions with suitable identification and rich covariates or justified effect-variation analysis. Machine-learning prediction is not causal evidence by itself; do not present this as a general prerequisite for predictive ML.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Advanced optional route for causal-effect questions with suitable identification and rich covariates or justified effect-variation analysis. Machine-learning prediction is not causal evidence by itself; do not present this as a general prerequisite for predictive ML.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS', 'DIME_AI', 'NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON', 'WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION', 'DOUBLEML_CAUSAL_ML_TUTORIAL']::text[], '[{"id":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","region":"International economics research; examples/method debate not a universal protocol","evidenceType":null},{"id":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","region":"Global unit; specific examples include United States data","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON","title":"Taming the Curse of Dimensionality: Quantitative Economics with Deep Learning","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w33117","region":"International scholarly working paper","evidenceType":null},{"id":"WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION","title":"Impact Evaluation in Practice, 2nd edition","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/sief-trust-fund/publication/impact-evaluation-in-practice","region":"Global development-practice learning resource","evidenceType":null},{"id":"DOUBLEML_CAUSAL_ML_TUTORIAL","title":"DoubleML: Introduction to Causal ML and Double ML","url":"https://docs.doubleml.org/tutorial/stable/lectures/L1/introduction_part1.html","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","locator":"Causal identification, supplementary robustness/sensitivity checks, external validity, and ML methods for causal effects","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","locator":"Examples of AI methods for timely labor-market measurement from social-media disclosures and GenAI access to development research","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON","title":"Taming the Curse of Dimensionality: Quantitative Economics with Deep Learning","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w33117","locator":"2024 working paper on quantitative economics/deep learning; working-paper status and authors’ caveat apply","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","locator":"Causal identification, supplementary robustness/sensitivity checks, external validity, and ML methods for causal effects","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"WB_IMPACT_EVALUATION","title":"Impact Evaluation in Practice, 2nd edition","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/sief-trust-fund/publication/impact-evaluation-in-practice","locator":"Parts on evaluation questions, causal methods, implementation, sampling, data collection, ethics and dissemination; Chapters 3–11 include identification designs","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"DOUBLEML_CAUSAL_ML_TUTORIAL","title":"DoubleML: Introduction to Causal ML and Double ML","url":"https://docs.doubleml.org/tutorial/stable/lectures/L1/introduction_part1.html","locator":"Course introduction, predictive-versus-causal modelling, Double Machine Learning and hands-on examples","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Do not use ML prediction as a substitute for causal identification.","Small samples, poor overlap, leakage, and model selection can undermine estimates.","Advanced method; no claim of universal occupational requirement.","Advanced optional route for causal-effect questions with suitable identification and rich covariates or justified effect-variation analysis. Machine-learning prediction is not causal evidence by itself; do not present this as a general prerequisite for predictive ML."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://docs.doubleml.org/tutorial/stable/lectures/L1/introduction_part1.html', 'DoubleML: Introduction to Causal ML and Double ML', '{"source_id":"DOUBLEML_CAUSAL_ML_TUTORIAL","title":"DoubleML: Introduction to Causal ML and Double ML","url":"https://docs.doubleml.org/tutorial/stable/lectures/L1/introduction_part1.html","publisher":"DoubleML project","locator":"Course introduction, predictive-versus-causal modelling, Double Machine Learning and hands-on examples","what_it_teaches":"Distinguishes prediction from causal questions and introduces DoubleML with applied examples, including heterogeneous effects and sensitivity analysis.","accessed":"2026-10-12","cost_access":"Free online course/tutorial; advanced material assumes causal and statistical preparation.","language":"English","level":"Advanced"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://docs.doubleml.org/tutorial/stable/lectures/L1/introduction_part1.html","locator":"Course introduction, predictive-versus-causal modelling, Double Machine Learning and hands-on examples","supports":"Distinguishes prediction from causal questions and introduces DoubleML with applied examples, including heterogeneous effects and sensitivity analysis.","access":"Free online course/tutorial; advanced material assumes causal and statistical preparation."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","region":"International economics research; examples/method debate not a universal protocol","evidenceType":null},{"id":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","region":"Global unit; specific examples include United States data","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON","title":"Taming the Curse of Dimensionality: Quantitative Economics with Deep Learning","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w33117","region":"International scholarly working paper","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","locator":"Causal identification, supplementary robustness/sensitivity checks, external validity, and ML methods for causal effects","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","locator":"Examples of AI methods for timely lab