ww.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","region":"Global unit; specific examples include United States data","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON","title":"Taming the Curse of Dimensionality: Quantitative Economics with Deep Learning","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w33117","region":"International scholarly working paper","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"AEA_CAUSAL_ECONOMETRICS","title":"The State of Applied Econometrics: Causality and Policy Evaluation","url":"https://pubs.aeaweb.org/doi/10.1257/jep.31.2.3","locator":"Causal identification, supplementary robustness/sensitivity checks, external validity, and ML methods for causal effects","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","locator":"Examples of AI methods for timely labor-market measurement from social-media disclosures and GenAI access to development research","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"NBER_DEEP_LEARNING_ECON","title":"Taming the Curse of Dimensionality: Quantitative Economics with Deep Learning","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w33117","locator":"2024 working paper on quantitative economics/deep learning; working-paper status and authors’ caveat apply","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078-ECON-CAUSAL-ML"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', 'Advanced', 'English', 'Free online course/tutorial; advanced material assumes causal and statistical preparation.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'economics-applied-analysis', 'optional', 'Advanced optional route for causal-effect questions with suitable identification and rich covariates or justified effect-variation analysis. Machine-learning prediction is not causal evidence by itself; do not present this as a gen