('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-ECON-LLM-EVIDENCE-SYNTHESIS', 'AI-assisted economic evidence discovery and synthesis with source verification', 'A supervised use of search/LLM tools to help find, organize, or summarize economic studies and policy documents while verifying every substantive claim against the cited original source.', 'May reduce clerical work in evidence review, but cannot replace systematic search protocols, quality appraisal, or reading the original research. Create a search log and evidence matrix with verified bibliographic records, study design, population, result, caveats, and human-checked source locators. Optional new technology edge, not a programme outcome or certification. Route note: Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Create a search log and evidence matrix with verified bibliographic records, study design, population, result, caveats, and human-checked source locators. Guardrail: LLMs may invent or misstate sources and findings. Do not treat generated summaries as evidence or skip original-source verification.', 'Create a search log and evidence matrix with verified bibliographic records, study design, population, result, caveats, and human-checked source locators.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Create a search log and evidence matrix with verified bibliographic records, study design, population, result, caveats, and human-checked source locators. Guardrail: LLMs may invent or misstate sources and findings. Do not treat generated summaries as evidence or skip original-source verification.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['DIME_AI', 'WB_REPRODUCIBLE', 'UNESCO_GENAI']::text[], '[{"id":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","region":"Global unit; specific examples include United States data","evidenceType":null},{"id":"WB_REPRODUCIBLE","title":"Guidance to Authors: Reproducible Research Repository","url":"https://worldbank.github.io/wb-reproducible-research-repository/guidance_note_wb.html","region":"World Bank publication policy, not universal law","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UNESCO_GENAI","title":"Guidance for generative AI in education and research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/guidance-generative-ai-education-and-research","region":"International guidance","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","locator":"Examples of AI methods for timely labor-market measurement from social-media disclosures and GenAI access to development research","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"WB_REPRODUCIBLE","title":"Guidance to Authors: Reproducible Research Repository","url":"https://worldbank.github.io/wb-reproducible-research-repository/guidance_note_wb.html","locator":"Requirements/guidance for empirical research reproducibility packages and transparency; as of Sep 2025 policy-research-paper rule stated","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UNESCO_GENAI","title":"Guidance for generative AI in education and research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/guidance-generative-ai-education-and-research","locator":"Human-centred guidance including data privacy, research capacity and safeguards","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UNESCO_GENAI","title":"Guidance for generative AI in education and research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/guidance-generative-ai-education-and-research","locator":"Human-centred guidance including data privacy, research capacity and safeguards","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"DIME_AI","title":"Artificial Intelligence and Development Impact Evaluation","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/impactevaluation/ai","locator":"Examples of AI methods for timely labor-market measurement from social-media disclosures and GenAI access to development research","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"WB_REPRODUCIBLE","title":"Guidance to Authors: Reproducible Research Repository","url":"https://worldbank.github.io/wb-reproducible-research-repository/guidance_note_wb.html","locator":"Requirements/guidance for empirical research reproducibility packages and transparency; as of Sep 2025 policy-research-paper rule stated","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["LLMs may invent or misstate sources and findings.","Do not treat generated summaries as evidence or skip original-source verification.","Emerging workflow; safeguards and model terms change.","Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Create a search log and evidence matrix with verified bibliographic records, study design, population, result, caveats, and human-checked source locators. Guardrail: LLMs may invent or misstate sources and findings. Do not treat generated summaries as evidence or skip original-source verification."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://worldbank.github.io/wb-reproducible-research-repository/guidance_note_wb.html', 'Guidance to Authors: Reproducible Research Repository', '{"source_id":"WB_REPRODUCIBLE","publisher":"World Bank Development Economics","title":"Guidance to Authors: Reproducible Research Repository","url":"https://worldbank.github.io/wb-reproducible-research-repository/guidance_note_wb.html","locator":"Requirements/guidance for empirical research reproducibility packages and transparency; as of Sep 2025 policy-research-paper rule stated","jurisdiction":"World Bank publication policy, not universal law","evidence_use":"Concrete institutional example of reproducible research expectations; not universal requirement for all r