('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-ECON-FORECASTING-UNCERTAINTY', 'Economic forecasting, scenario analysis, and forecast evaluation', 'Methods for projecting economic measures under stated assumptions and comparing possible paths rather than claiming certainty about the future.', 'Used in macroeconomic, sector, budget, and market analysis; forecast tasks differ from causal evaluation and descriptive trend reporting. Specify target, horizon, data vintage, baseline, model and assumptions; compare forecast with later observations and explain error and uncertainty. No programme instruction asserted. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Specify target, horizon, data vintage, baseline, model and assumptions; compare forecast with later observations and explain error and uncertainty. Guardrail: Forecasts can fail under shocks, revisions, regime changes, or model misspecification. Backtesting does not guarantee future performance.', 'Specify target, horizon, data vintage, baseline, model and assumptions; compare forecast with later observations and explain error and uncertainty.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Specify target, horizon, data vintage, baseline, model and assumptions; compare forecast with later observations and explain error and uncertainty. Guardrail: Forecasts can fail under shocks, revisions, regime changes, or model misspecification. Backtesting does not guarantee future performance.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ONET_ECONOMIST', 'NISER_EIR_2026', 'NISER_MACRO_MODEL', 'CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS']::text[], '[{"id":"ONET_ECONOMIST","title":"Economists, 19-3011.00","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link/details/19-3011.00","region":"United States","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NISER_EIR_2026","title":"NISER