('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-ECON-DISTRIBUTIONAL-ANALYSIS', 'Inequality, poverty, and distributional analysis', 'A set of approaches for describing how income, consumption, opportunity, or other defined resources/outcomes are distributed across people or groups.', 'Connects economic outcomes to distribution and welfare; the choice between income, consumption, services, or multidimensional poverty is substantive, not just technical. Select a defensible welfare measure and population, compute and visualize relevant distribution indicators, compare groups/time with uncertainty, and explain what the measure omits. No curriculum coverage inferred. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Select a defensible welfare measure and population, compute and visualize relevant distribution indicators, compare groups/time with uncertainty, and explain what the measure omits. Guardrail: No single measure captures all welfare or inequality. Comparisons require harmonized definitions, prices, sampling, and weights.', 'Select a defensible welfare measure and population, compute and visualize relevant distribution indicators, compare groups/time with uncertainty, and explain what the measure omits.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Select a defensible welfare measure and population, compute and visualize relevant distribution indicators, compare groups/time with uncertainty, and explain what the measure omits. Guardrail: No single measure captures all welfare or inequality. Comparisons require harmonized definitions, prices, sampling, and weights.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS', 'NBS_NLFS', 'NISER_EIR_2026', 'CORE_PYTHON_WELLBEING']::text[], '[{"id":"CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS","title":"Doing Economics","url":"