 applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Select a defensible welfare measure and population, compute and visualize relevant distribution indicators, compare groups/time with uncertainty, and explain what the measure omits. Guardrail: No single measure captures all welfare or inequality. Comparisons require harmonized definitions, prices, sampling, and weights.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-ECON-NIGERIA-MICRODATA', 'Use Nigerian official survey and macroeconomic data with design-aware interpretation', 'A research workflow using official Nigerian data catalogues/reports such as NBS labour force, CPI, GDP and other survey data, with each series� definition and access conditions checked.', 'Provides Nigeria-relevant empirical context, while the same statistical/economic methods can also be used on global datasets; availability of a local series is not proof of every task�s local labour-market demand. Download or access an identified release, record the study ID, period, variables, weights, methodology, and access terms, then produce a reproducible descriptive/economic analysis. Provides Nigeria-relevant empirical context, while the same statistical/economic methods can also be used on global datasets; availability of a local series is not proof of every task’s local labour-market demand. A Nigeria-context data resource, not a claim that any particular programme teaches its analysis. Route note: Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Download or access an identified release, record the study ID, period, variables, weights, methodology, and access terms, then produce a reproducible descriptive/economic analysis. Guardrail: Do not combine indicators with incompatible definitions or periods. Microdata access, revisions, weights, and documentation must be checked for each release.', 'Download or access an identified release, record the study ID, period, variables, weights, methodology, and access terms, then produce a reproducible descriptive/economic analysis.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected economics applied analysis area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Download or access an identified release, record the study ID, period, variables, weights, methodology, and access terms, then produce a reproducible descriptive/economic analysis. Guardrail: Do not combine indicators with incompatible definitions or periods. Microdata access, revisions, weights, and documentation must be checked for each release.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['NBS_CATALOG', 'NBS_NLFS', 'AFROBAROMETER_NIGERIA', 'NISER_EIR_2026', 'CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS']::text[], '[{"id":"NBS_CATALOG","title":"NBS Microdata Data Catalog","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog","region":"Nigeria; official statistical source","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_NLFS","title":"Nigeria Labour Force Survey (Q2 2024–Q2 2025)","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/152/search","region":"Nigeria; named survey rounds","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AFROBAROMETER_NIGERIA","title":"Survey resources and data: Nigeria","url":"https://www.afrobarometer.org/surveys-and-methods/survey-resources/?hidden-current-page=1&select-countries%5B%5D=nigeria","region":"Nigeria within a multi-country African survey programme","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NISER_EIR_2026","title":"NISER Economic Intelligence Report 2026","url":"https://niser.gov.ng/v2/niser-economic-intelligence-report-2026/","region":"Nigeria; 2026 report","evidenceType":null},{"id":"CORE_DOING_ECONOMICS","title":"Doing Economics","url":"https://www.core-econ.org/project/doing-economics/","region":"Global open educational resource","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"NBS_CATALOG","title":"NBS Microdata Data Catalog","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog","locator":"Catalog includes CPI, GDP, Nigeria Labour Force Survey and other surveys; each study has its own documentation/access details","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_NLFS","title":"Nigeria Labour Force Survey (Q2 2024–Q2 2025)","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/152/search","locator":"NBS study page, producer, study ID NGA-NBS-NLFS-Q22024-v1.0, documentation and data