descriptive/economic analysis. Guardrail: Do not combine indicators with incompatible definitions or periods. Microdata access, revisions, weights, and documentation must be checked for each release.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078-ECON-NATIONAL-ACCOUNTS-MEASUREMENT', 'National-accounts concepts and indicator interpretation', 'Knowledge of how measures such as output, value added, income, consumption and investment are defined and related within a national accounting framework.', 'Supports applied economic analysis of aggregate and sector-level change. It is not an instruction to compile official accounts; that work follows statistical standards and national implementation processes. Explain what a GDP or sector indicator does and does not count, identify the source and classification vintage, and produce a comparison that respects coverage and revisions. Area enrichment; specific national-account topics are not assumed to be taught by a programme unless its curriculum supports them. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Explain what a GDP or sector indicator does and does not count, identify the source and classification vintage, and produce a comparison that respects coverage and revisions. Guardrail: The 2025 SNA has been adopted internationally, but transition does not mean every national dataset or release has been rebased or implemented to it. Nigeria''s current published GDP methodology page identifies 2008 SNA; follow the actual Nigerian series methodology rather than silently relabeling it.', 'Explain what a GDP or sector indicator does and does not count, identify the source and classification vintage, and produce a comparison that respects coverage and revisions.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Explain what a GDP or sector indicator does and does not count, identify the source and classification vintage, and produce a comparison that respects coverage and revisions. Guardrail: The 2025 SNA has been adopted internationally, but transition does not mean every national dataset or release has been rebased or implemented to it. Nigeria''s current published GDP methodology page identifies 2008 SNA; follow the actual Nigerian series methodology rather than silently relabeling it.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UN_2025_SNA', 'NBS_GDP_METHODOLOGY', 'UN_SNA_CAPACITY_RESOURCES']::text[], '[{"id":"UN_2025_SNA","title":"System of National Accounts 2025","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/nationalaccount/sna2025.asp","region":"International statistical standard, jointly published by ISWGNA organizations","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GDP_METHODOLOGY","title":"GDP Methodology: Quarterly National Accounts","url":"https://nigerianstat.gov.ng/page/gdp-methodology","region":"Nigeria official economic statistics","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UN_SNA_CAPACITY_RESOURCES","title":"National Accounts Capacity Building Resources","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/nationalaccount/","region":"International official statistical guidance","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UN_2025_SNA","title":"System of National Accounts 2025","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/nationalaccount/sna2025.asp","locator":"Adoption, version status, introduction to updates for digitalization, globalization, informal economy, Islamic finance, and well-being/sustainability; adopted at UN Statistical Commission 56th session in 2025","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GDP_METHODOLOGY","title":"GDP Methodology: Quarterly National Accounts","url":"https://nigerianstat.gov.ng/page/gdp-methodology","locator":"Methodological notes identify SNA 2008, ISIC Rev. 4 and data sources/methodological pillars used in Nigerian GDP compilation","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UN_2025_SNA","title":"System of National Accounts 2025","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/nationalaccount/sna2025.asp","locator":"Adoption, version status, introduction to updates for digitalization, globaliz