idenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GDP_METHODOLOGY","title":"GDP Methodology: Quarterly National Accounts","url":"https://nigerianstat.gov.ng/page/gdp-methodology","region":"Nigeria official economic statistics","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UN_2025_SNA","title":"System of National Accounts 2025","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/nationalaccount/sna2025.asp","locator":"Adoption, version status, introduction to updates for digitalization, globalization, informal economy, Islamic finance, and well-being/sustainability; adopted at UN Statistical Commission 56th session in 2025","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"NBS_GDP_METHODOLOGY","title":"GDP Methodology: Quarterly National Accounts","url":"https://nigerianstat.gov.ng/page/gdp-methodology","locator":"Methodological notes identify SNA 2008, ISIC Rev. 4 and data sources/methodological pillars used in Nigerian GDP compilation","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078-ECON-NATIONAL-ACCOUNTS-MEASUREMENT"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free learning resource; review the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'economics-applied-analysis', 'useful', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Explain what a GDP or sector indicator does and does not count, identify the source and classification vintage, and produce a comparison that respects coverage and revisions. Guardrail: The 2025 SNA has been adopted internationally, but transition does not mean every national dataset or release has been rebased or implemented to it. Nigeria''s current published GDP methodology page identifies 2008 SNA; follow the actual Nigerian series methodology rather than silently relabeling it.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-ECON-LABOUR-STATISTICS', 'Labour-market measurement and interpretation', 'A design-aware approach to interpreting employment, unemployment, labour-force participation, underutilization and related work indicators using the definitions and survey documentation in force for the dataset.', 'Used in labour and development economics to describe access to work and labour-market change; it requires interpreting official classifications rather than treating a headline rate as the whole labour market. Compare labour outcomes only after checking the reference period, age/population scope, definitions, survey design, weights and standards implementation; produce a caveated table or policy brief. Optional economics area enrichment, not asserted as a curriculum outcome. Route note: Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Compare labour outcomes only after checking the reference period, age/population scope, definitions, survey design, weights and standards implementation; produce a caveated table or policy brief. Guardrail: International standard definitions evolve; check whether and how the survey implements the relevant ICLS standards. Do not compare Nigerian and international headline rates without reconciling definitions, population coverage and reference periods.', 'Compare labour outcomes only after checking the reference period, age/population scope, definitions, survey design, weights and standards implementation; produce a caveated table or policy brief.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected economics applied analysis area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Compare labour outcomes only after checking the reference period, age/population scope, definitions, survey design, weights and standards implementation; produce a caveated table or policy brief. Guardrail: Interna