('subgroup', 'D078:economics-applied-analysis', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-ECON-CASEVO-LLM-SIM', 'Casevo LLM-agent social/economic simulation (experimental research option)', 'Casevo is an experimental Python framework for LLM-enabled multi-agent social simulation over complex networks; its paper and README describe illustrative applications, not a validated general economic forecasting system. The repository LICENSE says Apache-2.0, but pyproject.toml says MIT, so package/release reuse terms are not established.', 'An emerging cross-over for exploring hypothetical decision processes or social-economic interaction. It does not show what Nigerian consumers/workers will do, replace survey/economic evidence, or qualify as a standard tool economists must learn. Experimental optional edge only; not a programme outcome, endorsed model, or credential. Route note: Experimental optional reading/tutorial route for LLM-enabled social/economic simulation. Do not treat outputs as observations, forecasts, established professional practice or validated claims about Nigerian populations. Package reuse/licence, runtime compatibility, API access, privacy terms and execution cost are not cleared; do not instruct learners to install or submit sensitive data.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Experimental optional reading/tutorial route for LLM-enabled social/economic simulation. Do not treat outputs as observations, forecasts, established professional practice or validated claims about Nigerian populations. Package reuse/licence, runtime compatibility, API access, privacy terms and execution cost are not cleared; do not instruct learners to install or submit sensitive data.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CASEVO_PAPER', 'CASEVO_REPOSITORY', 'LLM_HUMAN_PARTICIPANT_DIVERSITY', 'UNESCO_GENAI', 'MESA_DOCS']::text[], '[{"id":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19498","region":"International research preprint","evidenceTyp