M use as simulated participants across replications; identifies diversity limitations","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UNESCO_GENAI","title":"Guidance for generative AI in education and research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/guidance-generative-ai-education-and-research","locator":"Human-centred guidance including data privacy, research capacity and safeguards","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_REPOSITORY","title":"Casevo repository, README, LICENSE, pyproject.toml and releases","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README §§3–4: Python >=3.11, wheel-install instructions, U.S. 2020 election-debate example and Baichuan API_KEY requirement; root LICENSE: Apache License 2.0; pyproject.toml: version 0.3.19, Python >=3.11, Mesa==2.4.0, chromadb>=0.5.0, license text MIT; Releases page: v0.3.19 pre-release with three assets listed, asset metadata not inspected; PyPI project URL returned 404 on 2026-10-10","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MESA_DOCS","title":"Mesa: Agent-based modeling in Python","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/stable/index.html","locator":"Framework features, model/agent components, visualization, data collection and analysis","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_OFFICIAL_REPOSITORY_TUTORIAL","title":"Casevo: official getting-started tutorial and sample social simulation","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1-4: introduction, Mesa relationship, installation notes and step-by-step example simulation","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Evidence is an arXiv paper and evolving repository rather than a settled professional standard.","Repository LICENSE (Apache-2.0) conflicts with pyproject.toml package metadata (MIT); do not imply cleared package/release reuse terms.","README specifies Python >=3.11, Mesa 2.4.0 and ChromaDB >=0.5.0; the example requires a Baichuan API key. Installation/runtime, endpoint availability, charges and privacy terms were not tested or established.","Outputs can vary by model, prompts, and parameters and may reproduce stereotyped behavior.","Never treat synthetic agents as human observations.","Experimental optional reading/tutorial route for LLM-enabled social/economic simulation. Do not treat outputs as observations, forecasts, established professional practice or validated claims about Nigerian populations. Package reuse/licence, runtime compatibility, API access, privacy terms and execution cost are not cleared; do not instruct learners to install or submit sensitive data."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo', 'Casevo: official getting-started tutorial and sample social simulation', '{"source_id":"CASEVO_OFFICIAL_REPOSITORY_TUTORIAL","title":"Casevo: official getting-started tutorial and sample social simulation","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","publisher":"rgCASS Casevo project","locator":"README sections 1-4: introduction, Mesa relationship, installation notes and step-by-step example simulation","what_it_teaches":"How the Casevo tutorial assembles agents, model steps, prompts and a sample social simulation, then examines generated logs.","accessed":"2026-10-12","cost_access":"Free to read. Running the example requires a third-party LLM API key and may incur provider charges; package installation/reuse terms remain unresolved because repository and package metadata conflict.","language":"English","level":"Advanced/experimental"}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1-4: introduction, Mesa relationship, installation notes and step-by-step example simulation","supports":"How the Casevo tutorial assembles agents, model steps, prompts and a sample social simulation, then examines generated logs.","access":"Free to read. Running the example requires a third-party LLM API key and may incur provider charges; package installation/reuse terms remain unre