('subgroup', 'D078:human-geography-population', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078:human-geography-population:spatial-concepts-and-place', 'Spatial patterns, place and scale', 'Knowledge of how place, scale, location and spatial distribution affect a social question.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Human geography and population routes; spatial framing is useful only when place or location matters.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Human geography and population routes; spatial framing is useful only when place or location matters.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY', 'UNSD_CENSUS_2030']::text[], '[{"id":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","locator":"Table of Contents: Chapter 1 Introduction to Human Geography; Chapter 2 Population and Health; Chapter 3 Migration; Chapter 12 Human Settlements. Listing provides online and PDF formats under CC BY.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","locator":"Programme overview and Principles and Recommendations for Population and Housing Censuses, Revision 4: census as a primary source of disaggregated data; programme objectives include comparable, integrated and quality-assured census data.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","locator":"Table of Contents: Chapter 1 Introduction to Human Geography; Chapter 2 Population and Health; Chapter 3 Migration; Chapter 12 Human Settlements. Listing provides online and PDF formats under CC BY.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A map cannot make a weak construct valid or show causation.","Changing scale or boundaries can change the observed pattern.","Use a non-spatial table or qualitative place study when location is not material; map patterns do not establish causation.","Human geography and population routes; spatial framing is useful only when place or location matters."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography', 'Fundamentals of Human Geography', '{"source_id":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","publisher":"Open Textbook Library / University of Minnesota","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","locator":"Table of Contents: Chapter 1 Introduction to Human Geography; Chapter 2 Population and Health; Chapter 3 Migration; Chapter 12 Human Settlements. Listing provides online and PDF formats under CC BY.","what_it_teaches":"Human-geography chapters establish a people/place conceptual foundation; UN census guidance supports the relevance of disaggregated population data. Neither source makes spatial analysis necessary for every social question.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free; attribution license","limits":"Global introductory examples; supplement with current Nigerian data and local geography."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://open.u