('subgroup', 'D078:human-geography-population', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078:human-geography-population:spatial-data-provenance-scale', 'Spatial data provenance, geographic units and scale', 'The ability to check where spatial data came from, what geographic unit it represents, its date, coverage and scale, and whether the comparison is defensible.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Use when geographic units, coverage, reference period or map scale affect interpretation; inspect data access and anonymisation.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Use when geographic units, coverage, reference period or map scale affect interpretation; inspect data access and anonymisation.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UNSD_CENSUS_2030', 'NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24', 'QGIS_TRAINING']::text[], '[{"id":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","locator":"Programme overview and Principles and Recommendations for Population and Housing Censuses, Revision 4: census as a primary source of disaggregated data; programme objectives include comparable, integrated and quality-assured census data.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","locator":"Catalogue sections Identification, Version, Scope and Sampling: nationally representative panel of about 5,000 households and six geopolitical zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["Metadata checks do not repair biased or incomplete data.","Different boundaries can produce different patterns; no map is automatically neutral.","The GHS panel is not a census or a complete geographic register; inspect public-use access and anonymization before analysis.","Use when geographic units, coverage, reference period or map scale affect interpretation; inspect data access and anonymisation."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/', 'QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44', '{"source_id":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","publisher":"QGIS Project / Open Source Geospatial Foundation","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","what_it_teaches":"UN census programme standards and NBS survey metadata support checking geography, coverage, reference period and source design before comparing mapped observations. NBS metadata is a concrete Nigerian exercise source.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free documentation and exercises; QGIS is open-source software","limits":"Teaches software operations, not the validity of a social construct, local boundary authority, causal inference, or human-geography theory."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","supports":"UN census programme standards and NBS survey metadata support checking geography, coverage, reference period and source design before comparing mapped observations. NBS metadata is a concrete Nigerian exercise source.","access":"Free documentation and exercises; QGIS is open-source software"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","locator":"Programme overview and Principles and Recommendations f