, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","locator":"Programme overview and Principles and Recommendations for Population and Housing Censuses, Revision 4: census as a primary source of disaggregated data; programme objectives include comparable, integrated and quality-assured census data.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","locator":"Catalogue sections Identification, Version, Scope and Sampling: nationally representative panel of about 5,000 households and six geopolitical zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"UNSD_CENSUS_2030","title":"2030 World Population and Housing Census Programme","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic/sources/census/wphc/default.htm","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locato