yse data, final map).","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078:human-geography-population:qgis-spatial-tool"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free documentation and exercises; QGIS is open-source software', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'human-geography-population', 'optional', 'Optional tool for a justified spatial workflow; software operation does not validate the social question or geographic data.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:human-geography-population', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078:human-geography-population:spatial-pattern-communication', 'Explain spatial patterns without overclaiming', 'Communicate what a map or spatial table shows, what it does not show, and how scale, missingness and alternative explanations affect the conclusion.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Use when explaining a mapped pattern; state data, scale and uncertainty limits and avoid causal overclaiming.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Use when explaining a mapped pattern; state data, scale and uncertainty limits and avoid causal overclaiming.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['QGIS_TRAINING', 'OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY', 'NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24']::text[], '[{"id":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPEN_HUMAN_GEOGRAPHY","title":"Fundamentals of Human Geography","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/fundamentals-of-human-geography","locator":"Table of Contents: Chapter 1 Introduction to Human Geography; Chapter 2 Population and Health; Chapter 3 Migration; Chapter 12 Human Settlements. Listing provides online and PDF formats under CC BY.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","locator":"Catalogue sections Identification, Version, Scope and Sampling: nationally representative panel of about 5,000 households and six geopolitical zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","url":"https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/","locator":"Contents: 2 Creating and Exploring a Basic Map; 3 Classifying Vector Data; 4 Laying out the Maps; 6 Vector Analysis (reprojecting/transforming, vector analysis, network analysis, spatial statistics); 13 Assessment (base map, analyse data, final map).","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["Visual clarity can hide weak measurement or missing areas.","A local pattern is not automatically representative of every population or place.","A polished map is not proof of a mechanism or causal effect; state alternatives, uncertainty and data limitations.","Use when explaining a mapped pattern; state data, scale and uncertainty limits and avoid causal overclaiming."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://docs.qgis.org/3.44/en/docs/training_manual/', 'QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44', '{"source_id":"QGIS_TRAINING","title":"QGIS Training Manual, version 3.44","publisher":"QGIS Project / Open Source Geospatial Foundation","ur