l zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"UNSD_MIGRATION_STATS","title":"International migration statistics: methods and resources","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/sconcerns/migration/","locator":"Methods/resources list includes 2025 Recommendations on Statistics of International Migration and Temporary Mobility, 2025 data-integration materials, 2022 Indicators, and the 2022 Handbook on Measuring International Migration through Population Censuses; page describes stocks, flows, data quality and comparability.","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078:human-geography-population:census-survey-admin-appraisal"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Metadata free; microdata access is subject to the catalogue''s access conditions', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'human-geography-population', 'useful', 'Compare source design and coverage before using population evidence; a survey, census and administrative register are not interchangeable.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:human-geography-population', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078:human-geography-population:migration-urbanisation-interpretation', 'Interpret migration and urbanisation patterns', 'Relate migration, settlement and urban change to place, time and social/economic context while separating description from explanation.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Use when migration or settlement change is relevant; describe the population, period and source limits.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Use when migration or settlement change is relevant; describe the population, period and source limits.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UNSD_MIGRATION_STATS', 'NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24', 'OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE']::text[], '[{"id":"UNSD_MIGRATION_STATS","title":"International migration statistics: methods and resources","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/sconcerns/migration/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE","title":"Exploring how migration changes the places where we live","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UNSD_MIGRATION_STATS","title":"International migration statistics: methods and resources","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/sconcerns/migration/","locator":"Methods/resources list includes 2025 Recommendations on Statistics of International Migration and Temporary Mobility, 2025 data-integration materials, 2022 Indicators, and the 2022 Handbook on Measuring International Migration through Population Censuses; page describes stocks, flows, data quality and comparability.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","locator":"Catalogue sections Identification, Version, Scope and Sampling: nationally representative panel of about 5,000 households and six geopolitical zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE","title":"Exploring how migration changes the places where we live","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286","locator":"Course overview and sections on migration, cities, community, belonging, local authorities and inclusion; course text/videos explain how migration shapes places and communities.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE","title":"Exploring how migration changes the places where we live","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286","locator":"Course overview and sections on migration, cities, community, belonging, local authorities and inclusion; course text/videos explain how migration shapes places and communities.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["Migration association does not establish why people moved.","Urban categories and boundaries vary; international examples cannot be transferred uncritically to Nigeria.","OpenLearn examples are UK-based; migration trends and urban change require dated, population-specific data and competing explanations.","Use when migration or settlement change is relevant; describe the population, period and source limits."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286', 'Exploring how migration changes the places where we live', '{"source_id":"OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE","title":"Exploring how migration changes the places where we live","publisher":"The Open University, OpenLearn","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286","locator":"Course overview and sections on migration, cities, community, belonging, local authorities and inclusion; course text/videos explain how migration shapes places and communities.","what_it_teaches":"Current UNSD resources define stock/flow and data-quality scope; NBS provides Nigeria-specific migration modules; OpenLearn connects migration with place, community and belonging.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free OpenLearn learning resource","limits":"UK policy and city examples; use for concepts and interpretation, not Nigerian migration facts or statistical methods."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/course/view.php?id=14286","locator":"Course overview and sections on migration, cities, community, belonging, local authorities and inclusion; course text/videos explain how migration shapes places and communities.","supports":"Current UNSD resources define stock/flow and data-quality scope; NBS provides Nigeria-specific migration modules; OpenLearn connects migration with place, community and belonging.","access":"Free OpenLearn learning resource"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"UNSD_MIGRATION_STATS","title":"International migration statistics: methods and resources","url":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/sconcerns/migration/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPENLEARN_MIGRATION_PLACE","title":"Exploring how migration changes the places where we live","url":"h