('subgroup', 'D078:politics-governance-public-policy', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078-A03-knowledge-institutions-policy', 'Political institutions, public authority and policy process', 'Knowledge of who makes, implements and is affected by public decisions.', 'Map a public issue to the relevant institutions, decision points, affected groups and implementation responsibilities. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: Explain institutions, authority, policy stages and how responsibilities differ across actors; use Nigeria-specific institutional examples only where cited.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Explain institutions, authority, policy stages and how responsibilities differ across actors; use Nigeria-specific institutional examples only where cited.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ONET_POLSCI', 'UNESCO_ISCED', 'OSGF_PEAO', 'OPENLEARN_POLICY']::text[], '[{"id":"ONET_POLSCI","title":"Political Scientists, 19-3094.00","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link/details/19-3094.00","region":"United States","evidenceType":"occupational task framework"},{"id":"UNESCO_ISCED","title":"ISCED Fields of Education and Training 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","region":"global/international","evidenceType":"international education classification"},{"id":"OSGF_PEAO","title":"Political & Economic Affairs Office","url":"https://www.osgf.gov.ng/offices/political-economic-affairs-office/","region":"Nigeria","evidenceType":"government office mandate"},{"id":"OPENLEARN_POLICY","title":"Carrying out research for policy and advocacy work","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/society-politics-law/carrying-out-research-policy-and-advocacy-wor