('subgroup', 'D078:politics-governance-public-policy', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-A34-A03-competency-options-impact-analysis', 'Compare regulatory options and affected-group impacts', 'Use explicit objectives, feasible alternatives, affected-group evidence, expected effects and implementation constraints to make regulatory options comparable for an Area 3 policy decision.', 'Compare status quo, regulatory and non-regulatory choices, documenting assumptions, distributional effects, evidence quality and uncertainty. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: A specialist appraisal capability used within policy/RIA work, not a general claim of regulatory expertise.', NULL, 'build_next', 'A specialist appraisal capability used within policy/RIA work, not a general claim of regulatory expertise.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['A34_OECD_RIA', 'A34_NSIB_RIA', 'A34_OECD_DRAFT_NIGERIA_RIA']::text[], '[{"id":"A34_OECD_RIA","title":"Regulatory Impact Assessment","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/regulatory-impact-assessment_7a9638cb-en/full-report/component-5.html","region":"international comparative guidance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_NSIB_RIA","title":"Investigation Rulemaking Handbook, Issue 02 Revision 0","url":"https://edoc.nsib.gov.ng/app/static/images/Uploaded/Investigation_RuleMaking_Handbook_Issue_01_Rev_01_Sept_2023.pdf","region":"Nigeria; aviation safety investigation/rulemaking remit","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_OECD_DRAFT_NIGERIA_RIA","title":"Draft Good Practice Principles on the Effective Regulatory Governance of Large-Scale Food Fortification","url":"https://www.oecd.org/content/dam/oecd/en/events/public-consultations/2026/5/food-fortification-regulation/Draft%20Good%20Practice%20Principles%20FoFo%20Public%20Consultation.pdf","region":"international draft; Nigerian RIA Framework discussed; food-fortification policy example","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"A34_OECD_RIA","title":"Regulatory Impact Assessment","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/regulatory-impact-assessment_7a9638cb-en/full-report/component-5.html","locator":"Best practice principles for regulatory impact analysis; especially training/practical examples around lines/section discussing problem definition, objectives, alternatives, impact assessment, stakeholder engagement and implementation; monitoring/ex-post evaluation and review. Page components 5, section searched and opened 2026-10-10.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"A34_NSIB_RIA","title":"Investigation Rulemaking Handbook, Issue 02 Revision 0","url":"https://edoc.nsib.gov.ng/app/static/images/Uploaded/Investigation_RuleMaking_Handbook_Issue_01_Rev_01_Sept_2023.pdf","locator":"Official indexed handbook, printed p.25 of 94, section 3.4.6.1(g): the Rulemaking Committee drafts an RIA proposing alternatives for a Notice of Proposed Amendment, presents alternatives to the Director-General/CEO, and adapts the RIA after reviewing comments. The May 2023 handbook''s chapter 6 and Appendix J contain RIA methodology/form details.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"A34_OECD_DRAFT_NIGERIA_RIA","title":"Draft Good Practice Principles on the Effective Regulatory Governance of Large-Scale Food Fortification","url":"https://www.oecd.org/content/dam/oecd/en/events/public-consultations/2026/5/food-fortification-regulation/Draft%20Good%20Practice%20Principles%20FoFo%20Public%20Consultation.pdf","locator":"Draft PDF pp.14-15, paras 29-30 and Box 1.2: describes RIA as problem definition, multiple policy options, cost/benefit/other effects, implementation/monitoring/evaluation; reproduces Nigeria RIA Framework critical questions including non-regulatory option, consultation, impacts and unintended consequences.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"A34_OECD_RIA","title":"Regulatory Impact Assessment","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/regulatory-impact-assessment_7a9638cb-en/full-report/component-5.html","locator":"Best practice principles for regulatory impact analysis; especially training/practical examples around lines/section discussing problem definition, objectives, alternatives, impact assessment, stakeholder engagement and implementation; monitoring/ex-post evaluation and review. Page components 5, section searched and opened 2026-10-10.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["Chosen criteria and weights involve judgement","A complete-looking matrix can conceal missing evidence","Assessment does not confer regulatory authority or legal expertise","A specialist appraisal capability used within policy/RIA work, not a general claim of regulatory expertise."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/regulatory-impact-assessment_7a9638cb-en/full-report/component-5.html', 'Regulatory Impact Assessment', '{"source_id":"A34_OECD_RIA","publisher":"OECD","title":"Regulatory Impact Assessment","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/regulatory-impact-assessment_7a9638cb-en/full-report/component-5.html","exact_locator":"Best practice principles for regulatory impact analysis; especially training/practical examples around lines/section discussing problem definition, objectives, alternatives, impact assessment, stakeholder engagement and implementation; monitoring/ex-post evaluation and review. Page components 5, section searched and opened 2026-10-10.","source_family":"intergovernmental guidance/framework","jurisdiction":"international comparative guidance","evidence_strength":"authoritative method guidance; not binding law","supports":"RIA as structured options/effects/consultation analysis and connection to monitoring and review","limits":"OECD synthesis; country-specific law and institutional requirements differ; not a claim that all policy work requires RIA","access_date":"2