('subgroup', 'D078:politics-governance-public-policy', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078-A03-skill-validate-text-measures', 'Validate computational text labels against source context', 'The skill of checking whether categories or scores assigned to text actually capture the political or policy concept the researcher says they measure.', 'Compare labels/scores with human-reviewed examples, inspect error patterns and document how measurement choices affect conclusions. It is a specialist skill attached to computational text work, not a universal requirement for all areas. Not established. Route note: A specialist quality-control skill that supports computational policy-text analysis.', NULL, 'build_next', 'A specialist quality-control skill that supports computational policy-text analysis.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['GEORGETOWN_TEXT_AS_DATA', 'EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS', 'OXFORD_TEXT_AS_DATA']::text[], '[{"id":"GEORGETOWN_TEXT_AS_DATA","title":"PPOL 6801: Text as Data – Computational Linguistics","url":"https://tiagoventura.github.io/PPOL_6801/","region":"Global learning resource; course context is U.S. university policy school","evidenceType":null},{"id":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","region":"Global open course materials; examples and teaching context are Edinburgh","evidenceType":null},{"id":"OXFORD_TEXT_AS_DATA","title":"Text as Data: Computational Text Analysis","url":"https://github.com/aelshehawy/text-as-data-computational-text-analysis-oxford","region":"Global learning resource; course examples from Oxford political research","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"GEORGETOWN_TEXT_AS_DATA","title":"PPOL 6801: Text as Data – Computational Linguistics","url":"https://tiagoventura.github.io/PPOL_6801/","locator":"Course description: political speeches, government documents, social media and news; dictionary, se