09/National-Artificial-Intelligence-Strategy-19092025.pdf","locator":"Executive Summary, printed pp. 3–4, describes the strategy as a living document for Nigeria''s AI adoption and socio-economic context; Introduction, printed p. 8, notes governance concerns including ethical application, algorithmic transparency, data privacy and labour-market effects.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"UK_ATRS","title":"Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard Hub","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/algorithmic-transparency-recording-standard-hub","region":"United Kingdom public sector","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UK_ATRS","title":"Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard Hub","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/algorithmic-transparency-recording-standard-hub","locator":"Hub lines 86–96 and linked template/guidance: standardized public disclosure of how and why public bodies use algorithmic tools; applicability and mandatory scope are UK-specific.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"UK_ATRS","title":"Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard Hub","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/algorithmic-transparency-recording-standard-hub","region":"United Kingdom public sector","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NIGERIA_NATIONAL_AI_STRATEGY","title":"Nigeria National Artificial Intelligence Strategy, September 2025","url":"https://ncair.nitda.gov.ng/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/National-Artificial-Intelligence-Strategy-19092025.pdf","region":"Nigeria","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UK_ATRS","title":"Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard Hub","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/algorithmic-transparency-recording-standard-hub","locator":"Hub lines 86–96 and linked template/guidance: standardized public disclosure of how and why public bodies use algorithmic tools; applicability and mandatory scope are U