gic Foresight Toolkit for Resilient Public Policy","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/foresight-toolkit-for-resilient-public-policy_bcdd9304-en.html","locator":"2025 publication overview describes five-step foresight: challenge assumptions, explore evidence-based disruptions, create multiple scenarios, stress-test strategies and develop actionable plans; scenarios are possible futures, not predictions. PDF Module Three, printed p. 160, describes scenario construction as narrative exploration of possible conditions and consequences.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"OECD_FORESIGHT_TOOLKIT","title":"Strategic Foresight Toolkit for Resilient Public Policy","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/foresight-toolkit-for-resilient-public-policy_bcdd9304-en.html","region":"International public-policy practice","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"OECD_FORESIGHT_TOOLKIT","title":"Strategic Foresight Toolkit for Resilient Public Policy","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/foresight-toolkit-for-resilient-public-policy_bcdd9304-en.html","locator":"2025 publication overview describes five-step foresight: challenge assumptions, explore evidence-based disruptions, create multiple scenarios, stress-test strategies and develop actionable plans; scenarios are possible futures, not predictions. PDF Module Three, printed p. 160, describes scenario construction as narrative exploration of possible conditions and consequences.","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078-A03-method-policy-foresight-scenarios"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free learning resource; review the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'politics-governance-public-policy', 'optional', 'Optional planning method for uncertainty and long-term change in a specified policy area.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:politics-governance-public-policy', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A03-method-task-specific-ai-survey-workflow', 'Task-specific AI assistance in survey research', 'A survey workflow in which people choose a narrowly defined AI-supported task and test whether it performs adequately for the survey''s purpose before relying on it.', 'Use AI for a specified low-risk task such as draft-question critique or de-identified text organization, then test and document output before use. An area-specific extension for selected opinion/policy research, not a shared requirement across Social Sciences and Behavioural Research. No programme curriculum transfer is asserted in this area supplement. Route note: Optional and narrowly assigned AI help in survey work; the researcher remains responsible for instrument, sample, consent and interpretation.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional and narrowly assigned AI help in survey work; the researcher remains responsible for instrument, sample, consent and interpretation.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026', 'APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING']::text[], '[{"id":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Survey-Research.pdf","region":"International professional guidance, primarily U.S. survey-research context; not Nigerian regulation","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING","title":"Psychological Science Submission Guidelines: research transparency, online studies and research using LLMs","url":"https://www.psychologicalscience.org/publications/psychological_science/ps-submissions","region":"International journal policy from a U.S.-based scientific association; applies to its submissions, not a universal legal rule","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Resear