('subgroup', 'D078:politics-governance-public-policy', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-A03-competency-ai-survey-evaluation-and-disclosure', 'Evaluate and disclose the specific AI role in a survey', 'The ability to judge and explain an AI-supported survey step using evidence relevant to that exact task, rather than trusting fluent output or a vendor claim.', 'Record the AI task, evaluate validity/reliability/sensitivity/performance for that use, document human checks and disclose material use to relevant audiences. A specialist evidence-quality capability attached to survey/AI tasks; it does not make AI itself a general social-science competence requirement. No curriculum transfer is asserted. Route note: A safeguard attached to an AI-assisted survey workflow, not an independent AI credential.', NULL, 'build_next', 'A safeguard attached to an AI-assisted survey workflow, not an independent AI credential.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026', 'APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING']::text[], '[{"id":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Survey-Research.pdf","region":"International professional guidance, primarily U.S. survey-research context; not Nigerian regulation","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING","title":"Psychological Science Submission Guidelines: research transparency, online studies and research using LLMs","url":"https://www.psychologicalscience.org/publications/psychological_science/ps-submissions","region":"International journal policy from a U.S.-based scientific association; applies to its submissions, not a universal legal rule","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_SURVEY_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Survey-Research.pdf","l