('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078-A04-knowledge-behavioural-constructs', 'Social-behavioural concepts and construct meaning', 'Knowledge of how concepts such as attitudes, identity, group processes, norms and interaction are defined in a particular study.', 'Define a behavioural concept, distinguish it from neighbouring ideas and state what observable evidence could represent it. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: Understand what concepts such as attitude, identity, norm, motivation or wellbeing mean in a particular study; do not treat them as diagnoses by default.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Understand what concepts such as attitude, identity, norm, motivation or wellbeing mean in a particular study; do not treat them as diagnoses by default.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['APA_GUIDELINES', 'OPENSTAX_PSYCH_SOCIAL', 'UNESCO_ISCED']::text[], '[{"id":"APA_GUIDELINES","title":"Guidelines for the Undergraduate Psychology Major, Version 3.0","url":"https://www.apa.org/ed/precollege/undergraduate-major","region":"international professional body; U.S. association","evidenceType":"professional education guideline"},{"id":"OPENSTAX_PSYCH_SOCIAL","title":"Psychology 2e, Social Psychology chapter","url":"https://openstax.org/books/psychology-2e/pages/12-introduction","region":"U.S.-authored teaching examples; cross-cultural transfer must be tested","evidenceType":"free openly licensed university textbook section"},{"id":"UNESCO_ISCED","title":"ISCED Fields of Education and Training 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","region":"global/international","evidenceType":"international 