('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078-A04-skill-group-pattern-interpretation', 'Interpret group patterns without stereotyping individuals', 'Reading evidence about groups while keeping the inference at the level supported by the data and avoiding unsupported claims about individual people.', 'Report observed group patterns, uncertainty, alternative explanations and within-group variation in plain language. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: Interpret patterns at the level supported by the data and avoid turning group averages into claims about every person.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Interpret patterns at the level supported by the data and avoid turning group averages into claims about every person.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AEA_PRINCIPLES', 'APA_GUIDELINES', 'OL_SOC_PSYCH']::text[], '[{"id":"AEA_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","region":"international association","evidenceType":"professional ethics guidance"},{"id":"APA_GUIDELINES","title":"Guidelines for the Undergraduate Psychology Major, Version 3.0","url":"https://www.apa.org/ed/precollege/undergraduate-major","region":"international professional body; U.S. association","evidenceType":"professional education guideline"},{"id":"OL_SOC_PSYCH","title":"Social psychology and politics","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/health-sports-psychology/social-psychology-and-politics/content-section-0?intro=1","region":"global teaching resource","evidenceType":"free university learning resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AEA_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","locator":"Systematic inquiry, competence, integrity, respect for people, common good/equity, limitations and cultu