('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-A04-tools-quantitative-alternatives', 'R, Python, SPSS or Stata as analysis alternatives', 'Different software routes for organising, analysing and presenting numerical social-behaviour data; they are alternatives selected by task, access, team and reproducibility needs.', 'Import a permitted dataset, clean/code variables, produce descriptive or inferential analysis and document reproducible steps in a selected tool. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: R, Python, SPSS and Stata are alternative tools for preparing, analysing and presenting quantitative data; learners select according to task, access, course/employer context and future route.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'R, Python, SPSS and Stata are alternative tools for preparing, analysing and presenting quantitative data; learners select according to task, access, course/employer context and future route.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['DATACARPENTRY_SOCIAL_R', 'APA_GUIDELINES']::text[], '[{"id":"DATACARPENTRY_SOCIAL_R","title":"Data Carpentry lessons","url":"https://datacarpentry.org/lessons/","region":"global teaching resource","evidenceType":"free practical learning resource"},{"id":"APA_GUIDELINES","title":"Guidelines for the Undergraduate Psychology Major, Version 3.0","url":"https://www.apa.org/ed/precollege/undergraduate-major","region":"international professional body; U.S. association","evidenceType":"professional education guideline"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"DATACARPENTRY_SOCIAL_R","title":"Data Carpentry lessons","url":"https://datacarpentry.org/lessons/","locator":"Social Sciences workshop: data organisation, cleaning, analysis and visualisation with R; Python social-science materials marked alpha/development.","claimRole":"free practical learning resource"},{"sourceId":"NI