('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-A34-A04-competency-conflict-sensitivity', 'Assess how programme choices may affect conflict dynamics', 'Use a conflict analysis to check whether programme targeting, resource distribution, staffing, communication or engagement could intensify tensions or support constructive relations.', 'Write a risk-and-response note linking an evidenced context dynamic to a programme choice, mitigation, responsible actor and monitoring trigger. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: A specialist planning and review practice for programmes operating in conflict-affected or sensitive contexts.', NULL, 'build_next', 'A specialist planning and review practice for programmes operating in conflict-affected or sensitive contexts.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['A34_UNDP_CONFLICT_DEVELOPMENT', 'A34_UNDP_GENDER_CONFLICT', 'A34_UNSDG_CONFLICT_COURSE', 'A34_IPCR_RESEARCH_STRUCTURE', 'A34_IPCR_SCA']::text[], '[{"id":"A34_UNDP_CONFLICT_DEVELOPMENT","title":"Conducting a Conflict and Development Analysis","url":"https://www.undp.org/publications/conducting-conflict-and-development-analysis","region":"international; UN programming use","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_UNDP_GENDER_CONFLICT","title":"Gender-responsive conflict analysis for development programming","url":"https://www.undp.org/publications/gender-responsive-conflict-analysis-development-programming","region":"international; development programming","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_UNSDG_CONFLICT_COURSE","title":"Introduction to risk-informed, conflict-sensitive and peacebuilding programming","url":"https://www.unsdglearn.org/courses/introduction-to-risk-informed-conflict-sensitive-and-peacebuilding-programming/","region":"international; UNICEF programme context","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_IPCR_