('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A34-A04-method-behavioural-insights-cycle', 'Behavioural insights diagnosis and intervention cycle', 'Move from a precisely specified behaviour to evidence about its psychological, social/cultural and environmental drivers, then design, implement and evaluate a context-fit response. This is an applied specialist task, not a claim that all Area 4 learners do behaviour-change work.', 'Define a behaviour, diagnose barriers/enablers using context evidence, design an intervention, plan delivery and evaluate feasibility, acceptability and effects. No direct curriculum transfer is asserted. D078 programme-to-domain evidence supplies route context; this area candidate is enrichment unless separately supported by programme evidence. Route note: Optional intervention-design method, strongest in the documented public-health use cases; adapt and re-evidence before other sectors.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional intervention-design method, strongest in the documented public-health use cases; adapt and re-evidence before other sectors.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['A34_WHO_BI_STEPS', 'A34_WHO_AFRICA_BI', 'A34_WHO_TAILOR_HEALTH', 'A34_WHO_EVALUATE_BI', 'A34_NIGERIA_NACA_SBC', 'A34_NIGERIA_BIRDLAB', 'A34_LEARN_SURREY_BI']::text[], '[{"id":"A34_WHO_BI_STEPS","title":"Principles and steps for applying a behavioural perspective to public health","url":"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/documents/bi-tag-technical-note1_principles-and-steps.pdf?sfvrsn=efdefb39_5","region":"international; public health","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_WHO_AFRICA_BI","title":"Mainstreaming Behavioural Insights in the African Region","url":"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/documents/oms-mainstreaming_bi_in_africa-web.pdf?sfvrsn=938dc1ea_3","region":"WHO African Region; health","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_WHO_TAILOR_HEALTH","title":"A guide to tailoring health programmes using behavioural and cultural insights","url":"https://www.who.int/europe/publications/i/item/9789289058919","region":"WHO European Region; health","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_WHO_EVALUATE_BI","title":"Evaluating the impact of interventions addressing health behaviour: considerations and tools for policy-makers","url":"https://www.who.int/europe/publications/i/item/WHO-EURO-2024-10200-49972-75147","region":"WHO European Region; health","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_NIGERIA_NACA_SBC","title":"National HIV Self-Testing and PrEP Communication Strategy 2022","url":"https://www.naca.gov.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/National-HIVST-and-PrEP-Communication-Strategy-2022_.pdf","region":"Nigeria; HIV prevention and health communication","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_NIGERIA_BIRDLAB","title":"NETBRECSIN Newsletter: Behavioural Insights Research and Design Laboratory","url":"https://health.gov.ng/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/NETBRECTSIN-Newsletter-Vol-6-No-2.pdf","region":"Nigeria; maternal/child health and WASH","evidenceType":null},{"id":"A34_LEARN_SURREY_BI","title":"Bitesize Behavioural Science Project video series","url":"https://www.surreyi.gov.uk/behavioural-science-turning-insights-to-action/","region":"UK local government","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"A34_WHO_BI_STEPS","title":"Principles and steps for applying a behavioural perspective to public health","url":"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/documents/bi-tag-technical-note1_principles-and-steps.pdf?sfvrsn=efdefb39_5","locator":"Technical note pp.1-5: six principles and five-step application; pp.2-4 cover psychological, social/cultural and environmental influences, evidence-led intervention design, contextual evaluation and participation/co-design.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"A34_WHO_AFRICA_BI","title":"Mainstreaming Behavioural Insights in the African Region","url":"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/documents/oms-mainstreaming_bi_in_africa-web.pdf?sfvrsn=938dc1ea_3"