::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free learning resource; review the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'psychology-social-behaviour', 'useful', 'Specialist evaluation competency for an intervention with a defined behaviour and setting.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A04-method-digital-trace-inquiry', 'Digital-trace and online-interaction research', 'Research using records created through digital activity—such as public posts, interaction logs or online communities—to examine a bounded social question.', 'Define the platform/source and interaction, establish provenance and lawful/ethical access, collect a bounded dataset and analyse patterns with coverage caveats. Area-specific application of the existing computational-social-research candidate; not a separate domain foundation item. No curriculum transfer is claimed. Route note: Optional method for suitable digital traces; platform users/data are not automatically representative of a population.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional method for suitable digital traces; platform users/data are not automatically representative of a population.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS', 'UKDS_TEXT_MINING_SOCIAL', 'AOIR_ETHICS_GUIDELINES', 'NDPC_ACT_NIGERIA']::text[], '[{"id":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","region":"Global open course materials; examples and teaching context are Edinburgh","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UKDS_TEXT_MINING_SOCIAL","title":"Computational Social Science learning hub: text-mining and web-scraping for social science","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/computational-social-science/","region":"UK learning service; methods are portable, source/platform and law are not","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AOIR_ETHICS_GUIDELINES","title":"Internet Research: Ethical Guidelines 3.0","url":"https://aoir.org/reports/ethics3.pdf","region":"International professional research-ethics guidance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NDPC_ACT_NIGERIA","title":"Nigeria Data Protection Act, 2023","url":"https://www.ndpc.gov.ng/ndp-act-2023/","region":"Nigeria","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","locator":"Learning outcomes and course outline lines 6–27: frame social-behaviour questions, select computational methods with ethics/bias in view, analyse text/network data, explain limitations; topics include machine learning, network/text analysis, LLMs, data collection and hands-on labs.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UKDS_TEXT_MINING_SOCIAL","title":"Computational Social Science learning hub: text-mining and web-scraping for social science","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/computational-social-science/","locator":"Text-mining section lines 110–114 lists social-science materials for NLP, sentiment, classifiers, named entities and social-network extraction. Web/API section lines 115–122 covers collection and explicitly notes some Twitter API tutorials are outdated while data handling/method content may remain useful.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AOIR_ETHICS_GUIDELINES","title":"Internet Research: Ethical Guidelines 3.0","url":"https://aoir.org/reports/ethics3.pdf","locator":"Guidelines 3.0: ethics is contextual and process-based across internet research; consider expectation of privacy, identifiability, vulnerability, platform context, data collection/reuse and researcher responsibility rather than assuming all publicly visible material is ethically free to use.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NDPC_ACT_NIGERIA","title":"Nigeria Data Protection Act, 2023","url":"https://www.ndpc.gov.ng/ndp-act-2023/","locator":"Official Act and NDPC resources; relevant checks include Act principles and lawful bases governing personal-data processing, data-subject rights, security and cross-border transfers. Consult the Act text and current NDPC guidance for the particular project rather than interpreting this summary as legal advice.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AOIR_ETHICS_GUIDELINES","title":"Internet Research: Ethical Guidelines 3.0","url":"https://aoir.org/reports/ethics3.pdf","locator":"Guidelines 3.0: ethics is contextual and process-based across internet research; consider expectation of privacy, identifiability, vulnerability, platform context, data collection/reuse and researcher responsibility rather than assuming all publicly visible material is ethically free to use.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","locator":"Learning outcomes and course outline lines 6–27: frame social-behaviour questions, select computational methods with ethics/bias in view, analyse text/network data, explain limitations; topics include machine learning, network/text analysis, LLMs, data collection and hands-on labs.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","locator":"Learning outcomes and course outline lines 6–27: frame social-behaviour questions, select computational methods with ethics/bias in view, analyse text/network data, explain limitations; topics include machine learning, network/text analysis, LLMs, data collection and hands-on labs.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["state","label","explanation","Optional method for suitable digital traces; platform users/data are not automatically representative of a population."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css', 'Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science', '{"source_id":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","publisher":"University of Edinburgh, School of Informatics and School of Political and Social Science","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Scien