('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A04-method-human-ai-social-interaction-study', 'Research human behaviour in AI-mediated interactions', 'A social-behaviour study where an AI system or AI-mediated platform is part of the interaction or setting being examined.', 'Study a bounded question about trust, advice, participation or behaviour in AI-mediated interaction using ethical human data and an appropriate comparison. An emerging specialization task that applies established survey, experiment, interview and observational methods to new human-AI settings. No curriculum connection claimed. Route note: Emerging topic applying established human-subject and social-interaction methods to people interacting with AI systems.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Emerging topic applying established human-subject and social-interaction methods to people interacting with AI systems.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS', 'EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS']::text[], '[{"id":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","region":"U.S. research sample; not Nigeria-representative","evidenceType":null},{"id":"EDINBURGH_CSS_OPEN_MATERIALS","title":"Understanding Society with Big Data: Computational Social Science","url":"https://opencourse.inf.ed.ac.uk/css","region":"Global open course materials; examples and teaching context are Edinburgh","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","locator":"Policy brief dated 2025-05-20: describes a study using interviews from 1,052 U.S. participants and comparing agent outputs against their later survey/experiment answers; warns about privacy, consent, over-reliance and that current architectures need further work before reliable u