('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A04-method-llm-social-agent-simulation-experimental', 'LLM social-agent simulation for exploratory theory testing (experimental)', 'A computer simulation in which language-model agents are given roles, memories or rules and interact within a researcher-defined social environment.', 'Specify agent assumptions and interaction rules, run a bounded simulation, inspect sensitivity and compare outputs with observed data or human studies where possible. It is a niche emerging application of existing D078 Mesa/Casevo and computational-social-research candidates; those tools are linked by ID and not duplicated here. No programme curriculum transfer claimed. Route note: Niche, emerging and explicitly experimental; appropriate for exploring hypotheses or design ideas before testing with human evidence.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Niche, emerging and explicitly experimental; appropriate for exploring hypotheses or design ideas before testing with human evidence.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CASEVO_PAPER', 'STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS', 'LLM_HUMAN_SURROGATE_CAUTION', 'CASEVO_PROJECT']::text[], '[{"id":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19498","region":"International research preprint","evidenceType":null},{"id":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","region":"U.S. research sample; not Nigeria-representative","evidenceType":null},{"id":"LLM_HUMAN_SURROGATE_CAUTION","title":"Take caution in using LLMs as human surrogates","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12184514/","region":"Study-specific empirical evidence; not a universal failure theorem for every model/task","evidenceType":null},{"id":"CASEVO_PROJECT","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","region":"Global open-source research software","evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19498","locator":"Abstract and paper on LLM-integrated multi-agent simulation for social phenomena; arXiv preprint, 2024","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","locator":"Policy brief dated 2025-05-20: describes a study using interviews from 1,052 U.S. participants and comparing agent outputs against their later survey/experiment answers; warns about privacy, consent, over-reliance and that current architectures need further work before reliable use.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"LLM_HUMAN_SURROGATE_CAUTION","title":"Take caution in using LLMs as human surrogates","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12184514/","locator":"Abstract/results: a controlled empirical case demonstrates model-generated responses can diverge systematically from human participant data; discusses reasoning, response-distribution and framing sensitivity, and risks of treating generated data as a substitute.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","locator":"Policy brief dated 2025-05-20: describes a study using interviews from 1,052 U.S. participants and comparing agent outputs against their later survey/experiment answers; warns about privacy, consent, over-reliance and that current architectures need further work before reliable use.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"LLM_HUMAN_SURROGATE_CAUTION","title":"Take caution in using LLMs as human surrogates","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12184514/","locator":"Abstract/results: a controlled empirical case demonstrates model-generated responses can diverge systematically from human participant data; discusses reasoning, response-distribution and framing sensitivity, and risks of treating generated data as a substitute.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CASEVO_PROJECT","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1–4: framework purpose is multi-agent social simulations on complex networks; built on Mesa; tutorial creates a basic model and describes Python >3.11, NetworkX, Matplotlib and LLM API integration; repository release history lists 0.3.19 dated 2025-04-22 and Apache-2.0 license.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["state","label","explanation","Niche, emerging and explicitly experimental; appropriate for exploring hypotheses or design ideas before testing with human evidence."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo', 'Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator', '{"source_id":"CASEVO_PROJECT","publisher":"rgCASS Casevo project contributors","title":"Casevo: Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","exact_locator":"README sections 1–4: framework purpose is multi-agent social simulations on complex networks; built on Mesa; tutorial creates a basic model and describes Python >3.11, NetworkX, Matplotlib and LLM API integration; repository release history lists 0.3.19 dated 2025-04-22 and Apache-2.0 license.","source_role":"tool_identity_and_free_task_specific_learning","jurisdiction":"Global open-source research software","supports":"A niche framework option for a carefully specified experimental social-simulation task; ties the existing domain Casevo candidate to an area-owned behavioural/political scenario use case.","limitations":"Young, specialist framework; code/project documentation does not validate its simulated population as representative or its outputs as evidence about real people. Requires Python, ABM/network concepts, model validation and possible LLM API costs. This is not a domain-wide requirement or a substitute for observed data/participants.","access_date":"2026-10-10","locator":"README sections 1–4: framework purpose is multi-agent social simulations on complex networks; built on Mesa; tutorial creates a basic model and describes Python >3.11, NetworkX, Matplotlib and LLM API integration; repository release history lists 0.3.19 dated 2025-04-22 and Apache-2.0 license."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://github.com/rgCASS/casevo","locator":"README sections 1–4: framework purpose is multi-agent social simulations on complex networks; built on Mesa; tutorial creates a basic model and describes Python >3.11, NetworkX, Matplotlib and LLM API integration; repository release history lists 0.3.19 dated 2025-04-22 and Apache-2.0 license.","supports":"A niche framework option for a carefully specified experimental social-simulation task; ties the existing domain Casevo candidate to an area-owned behavioural/political scenario use case.","access":null}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19498","region":"International research preprint","evidenceType":null},{"id":"STANFORD_GENERATIVE_AGENTS","title":"Simulating Human Behavior with AI Agents","url":"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/simulating-human-behavior-with-ai-agents","region":"U.S. research sample; not Nigeria-representative","evidenceType":null},{"id":"LLM_HUMAN_SURROGATE_CAUTION","title":"Take caution in using LLMs as human surrogates","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12184514/","region":"Study-specific empirical evidence; not a universal failure theorem for 