('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-A04-method-contextual-measure-adaptation', 'Contextual adaptation and validation of social-behaviour measures', 'A planned process for checking and, when needed, adapting a measure so its concepts, wording, response choices and use fit a target social and linguistic context.', 'Check construct relevance, permissions, translation, cognitive understanding, pilot performance and measurement properties before comparing scores. An area-specific method supporting credible behavioural evidence, not a clinical assessment or diagnosis method. No programme curriculum transfer is asserted. Route note: Use when adapting a social-behaviour measure for a new language, culture, population or setting; not a shortcut to clinical test approval.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Use when adapting a social-behaviour measure for a new language, culture, population or setting; not a shortcut to clinical test approval.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES', 'APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING']::text[], '[{"id":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","region":"International guidance; not law or a Nigeria-specific validation study","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING","title":"Psychological Science Submission Guidelines: research transparency, online studies and research using LLMs","url":"https://www.psychologicalscience.org/publications/psychological_science/ps-submissions","region":"International journal policy from a U.S.-based scientific association; applies to its submissions, not a universal legal rule","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","locator":"Official ITC guideline, 18 recommendations organized under preconditions, test development, confirmation, administration, scoring/interpretation and documentation; official overview at https://www.intestcom.org/page/14 explains that adaptation applies across cultural settings even without translation.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING","title":"Psychological Science Submission Guidelines: research transparency, online studies and research using LLMs","url":"https://www.psychologicalscience.org/publications/psychological_science/ps-submissions","locator":"Research Transparency Statement and Online Studies §§ (web page lines 267–336): disclose AI use; describe prevention/detection and limitations for AI-generated online responses. Research Using Machine Learning and LLMs §§ (lines 367–390): reporting, code, theoretical/method justification and limits on treating LLMs as model organisms/proxies.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","locator":"Official ITC guideline, 18 recommendations organized under preconditions, test development, confirmation, administration, scoring/interpretation and documentation; official overview at https://www.intestcom.org/page/14 explains that adaptation applies across cultural settings even without translation.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","locator":"Official ITC guideline, 18 recommendations organized under preconditions, test development, confirmation, administration, scoring/interpretation and documentation; official overview at https://www.intestcom.org/page/14 explains that adaptation applies across cultural settings even without translation.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["state","label","explanation","Use when adapting a social-behaviour measure for a new language, culture, population or setting; not a shortcut to clinical test approval."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf', 'ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition', '{"source_id":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","publisher":"International Test Commission (ITC)","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","exact_locator":"Official ITC guideline, 18 recommendations organized under preconditions, test development, confirmation, administration, scoring/interpretation and documentation; official overview at https://www.intestcom.org/page/14 explains that adaptation applies across cultural settings even without translation.","source_role":"international_professional_guideline_for_measurement_adaptation","jurisdiction":"International guidance; not law or a Nigeria-specific validation study","supports":"When social attitudes, identity, interaction or other constructs are measured across Nigerian language/cultural groups or compared with an external population, translation alone is insufficient; adapt, confirm, administer, interpret and document the instrument for its target context.","limitations":"Guidelines support responsible practice but do not by themselves validate a particular scale or prove measurement equivalence in Nigeria. The source concerns tests/instruments and must not be used to imply clinical assessment authority.","access_date":"2026-10-10","locator":"Official ITC guideline, 18 recommendations organized under preconditions, test development, confirmation, administration, scoring/interpretation and documentation; official overview at https://www.intestcom.or