('subgroup', 'D078:psychology-social-behaviour', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-A04-competency-measure-comparability-judgement', 'Judge when social-behaviour scores can be compared across groups', 'The ability to distinguish a difference in people''s measured scores from a difference caused by how a question or scale works across groups.', 'State which equivalence assumptions were examined, what evidence supports comparison and which group-level conclusions should be withheld. A specialist evidence-interpretation capability that strengthens social-behaviour inquiry and avoids false cultural generalization. No programme curriculum transfer is asserted. Route note: Advanced evidence-interpretation capability for cross-group or cross-context score comparison; not a basic prerequisite for all behavioural study.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Advanced evidence-interpretation capability for cross-group or cross-context score comparison; not a basic prerequisite for all behavioural study.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES', 'APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING', 'LAVAAN_MULTIGROUP_TUTORIAL']::text[], '[{"id":"ITC_TEST_ADAPTATION_GUIDELINES","title":"ITC Guidelines for Translating and Adapting Tests, Second Edition","url":"https://www.intestcom.org/files/guideline_test_adaptation_2ed.pdf","region":"International guidance; not law or a Nigeria-specific validation study","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APS_PSYCHOLOGICAL_SCIENCE_REPORTING","title":"Psychological Science Submission Guidelines: research transparency, online studies and research using LLMs","url":"https://www.psychologicalscience.org/publications/psychological_science/ps-submissions","region":"International journal policy from a U.S.-based scientific association; applies to its submissions, not a universal legal rule","evidenceType":null},{"id":"LAVAAN_MULTIGROUP_TUTORIAL","title":"Multiple groups and measurement invariance","url":"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html","region":"Global op