('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:study-question-design', 'Turn a social question into a feasible study design', 'The skill of defining the purpose, population, evidence, method, sampling, ethics and limits before collecting data.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Research/evaluation route; align the question, available evidence, method and feasible scope.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Research/evaluation route; align the question, available evidence, method and feasible scope.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK', 'MAGENTA_BOOK', 'SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT']::text[], '[{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","locator":"Evaluation Steps: assess context; describe the program; focus evaluation questions and design; gather credible evidence; generate and support conclusions; act on findings. The framework page identifies these steps as its evaluation process.","cl