ame, selection, response and weighting; measurement quality and sample size alone do not guarantee valid inference.","Use when selecting people/cases or measuring a concept; state who or what the evidence can represent."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/', 'Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition', '{"source_id":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","publisher":"Anol Bhattacherjee / University of Southern Queensland Open Textbooks","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","what_it_teaches":"Magenta Book''s sampling section distinguishes probability and non-probability samples, non-response and inference limits; textbook Chapters 6-8 cover measurement, reliability/validity and sampling. NBS metadata supplies a real sampling design example.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free open textbook; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","limits":"Compact foundational text; Chapter 16 includes Australian context and legal/institutional rules must be checked locally."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","supports":"Ma