('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'method', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:field-and-document-method-choice', 'Choose between surveys, interviews, focus groups and document methods', 'A method-choice process that matches the evidence source to the question, participants, setting, sensitivity and intended use.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Choose among surveys, interviews, focus groups or documents according to the question; these are alternatives, not a cumulative checklist.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Choose among surveys, interviews, focus groups or documents according to the question; these are alternatives, not a cumulative checklist.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT', 'CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK', 'AEA_COMPETENCIES']::text[], '[{"id":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AEA_COMPETENCIES","title":"AEA Evaluator Competencies","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Competencies-Standards/AEA-Evaluator-Competencies","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","locator":"Evaluation Steps: assess context; describe the program; focus evaluation questions and design; gather credible evidence; generate and support conclusions; act on findings. The framework page identifies these steps as its evaluation process.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AEA_COMPETENCIES","title":"AEA Evaluator Competencies","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Competencies-Standards/AEA-Evaluator-Competencies","locator":"Competency domains include methodology, context, planning/management and interpersonal practice; interpersonal domain names communication, facilitation and conflict resolution. The page describes a professional competency framework.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A method choice does not guarantee response quality, truthful answers or causal evidence.","Focus groups and interviews capture situated accounts, not automatically population prevalence.","Methods are not interchangeable; choose according to question, evidence, access, ethics and inference target. The source text is foundational r