('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:kobo-electronic-collection', 'KoboToolbox for electronic form collection', 'A digital form-collection platform that can support browser/mobile data capture, validation, offline workflows and export when the study design calls for it.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Optional form-collection tool after survey design, sampling, consent and data-protection decisions; Kobo does not make those decisions for the learner.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional form-collection tool after survey design, sampling, consent and data-protection decisions; Kobo does not make those decisions for the learner.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['KOBO_WEB_FORMS', 'KOBO_EXPORT']::text[], '[{"id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","locator":"Downloading your data and Export types sections: project DATA > Downloads workflow and XLS, CSV, GeoJSON and SPSS Labels formats; CSV is described for import into data-management software and GeoJSON for GIS integration.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["KoboToolbox does not make a questionnaire valid, a sample representative or an analysis correct.","Offline/device/export settings can create missingness or version problems; test before fieldwork.","Tool use follows a justified instrument and sampling plan; test skip/validation logic, security and offline synchronization before collecting real data.","Optional form-collection tool after survey design, sampling, consent and data-protection decisions; Kobo does not make those decisions for the learner."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html', 'Collecting data using web forms', '{"source_id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","publisher":"KoboToolbox Support","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","what_it_teaches":"Official Kobo documentation confirms form logic, validation, offline caching/queue behavior and data-export options, directly matching the implementation task.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free public documentation","limits":"Describes a platform implementation; test the actual device, project settings, security, consent flow and connectivity before field use."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","supports":"Official Kobo documentation confirms form logic, validation, offline caching/queue behavior and data-export options, directly matching the implementation task.","access":"Free public documentation"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":"item_identity"},{"sourceId":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","locator":"Downloading your data and Export types sections: project DATA > Downloads workflow and XLS, CSV, GeoJSON and SPSS Labels formats; CSV is described for import into data-management software and GeoJSON for GIS integration.","claimRole":"item_identity"}]},"checkpoint_fit":{"source_references":[{"id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"},{"sourceId":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","locator":"Downloading your data and Export types sections: project DATA > Downloads workflow and XLS, CSV, GeoJSON and SPSS Labels formats; CSV is described for import into data-management software and GeoJSON for GIS integration.","claimRole":"checkpoint_fit"}]},"plain_meaning":{"source_references":[{"id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"},{"sourceId":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","locator":"Downloading your data and Export types sections: project DATA > Downloads workflow and XLS, CSV, GeoJSON and SPSS Labels formats; CSV is described for import into data-management software and GeoJSON for GIS integration.","claimRole":"plain_meaning"}]},"contextual_use":{"source_references":[{"id":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"KOBO_WEB_FORMS","title":"Collecting data using web forms","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/data_through_webforms.html","locator":"Overview and Offline data collection sections: web forms support configured form logic including skip logic and validation; offline use requires opening and caching the form before disconnecting, with queued submissions uploading after reconnection.","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"KOBO_EXPORT","title":"Exporting and downloading your data","url":"https://support.kobotoolbox.org/export_download.html","locator":"Downloading your data and Export types sections: project DATA > Downloads workflow and XLS, CSV, GeoJSON and SPSS Labels formats; CSV is described for import into data-management software and GeoJSON for GIS integration.","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078:social-research-evaluation:kobo-electronic-collection"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free public documentation', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'social-research-evaluation', 'optional', 'Optional form-collection tool after survey design, sampling, consent and data-protection decisions; Kobo does not make those decisions for the learner.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'knowledge', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:programme-theory-and-logic', 'Describe how a programme is expected to produce change', 'Knowledge of programme context, activities, assumptions, outputs, outcomes and a logic model/theory of change.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Useful when an evaluation needs to explain how activities are expected to lead to change; not required for every descriptive study.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Useful when an evaluation needs to explain how activities are expected to lead to change; not required for every descriptive study.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['MAGENTA_BOOK', 'CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK', 'OPENLEARN_EVALUATION']::text[], '[{"id":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPENLEARN_EVALUATION","title":"Global challenges in practice: designing a development intervention","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=141129&section=3","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","locator":"Sections 2.2.1-2.2.2 on understanding an intervention, theory of change and evaluation purpose/questions; survey sampling section describes probability/non-probability sampling, representativeness and non-response; methods chapters cover evaluation design and evidence.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","locator":"Evaluation Steps: assess context; describe the program; focus evaluation questions and design; gather credible evidence; generate and support conclusions; act on findings. The framework page identifies these steps as its evaluation process.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENLEARN_EVALUATION","title":"Global challenges in practice: designing a development intervention","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=141129&section=3","locator":"Week 3 section 2, Why is evaluation important?; adjacent course sections distinguish monitoring and evaluation and discuss indicator choice. The course page identifies this as a free, 12-hour intermediate course.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["A logic model describes an intended pathway; it does not prove that the pathway worked.","Theory of change must be tested against context and implementation evidence.","A logic model records an explicit programme theory; it does not prove that the causal chain operates or that outcomes were caused by the programme.","Useful when an evaluation needs to explain how activities are expected to lead to change; not required for every descriptive study."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=141129&section=3', 'Global challenges in practice: designing a development intervention', '{"source_id":"OPENLEARN_EVALUATION","title":"Global challenges in practice: designing a development intervention","publisher":"The Open University, OpenLearn","url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=141129&section=3","locator":"Week 3 section 2, Why is evaluation important?; adjacent course sections distinguish monitoring and evaluation and discuss indicator choice. The course page identifies this as a free, 12-hour intermediate course.","what_it_teaches":"Magenta Book sections 2.2.1-2.2.2 describe theory of change, causal steps, assumptions, context, stakeholder testing and evaluation questions; CDC places programme description before question/design and evidence.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free course; free account for course tracking/participation statement","limits":"Development-intervention context; introductory orientation rather than a full design manual."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=141129&section=3","locator":"Week 3 section 2, Why is evaluation important?; adjacent course sections distinguish monitoring and evaluation and discuss indicator choice. The course page identifies this as a free, 12-hour intermediate course.","supports":"Magenta Book sections 2.2.1-2.2.2 describe theory of change, causal steps, assumptions, context, stakeholder testing and evaluation questions; CDC places programme description before question/design and evidence.","access":"Free course; free account for course tracking/participation statement"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'subgroup', '2026-10-12', 'approved', '{"claims":{"item_identity":{"source_references":[{"id":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Gove