('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'skill', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:stakeholder-use-and-reporting', 'Turn findings into usable, transparent recommendations', 'The skill of reporting evidence, uncertainty, context and recommendations for the people who will use the evaluation.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Explain findings and recommendations for the intended users while separating evidence from judgement and uncertainty.', NULL, 'build_next', 'Explain findings and recommendations for the intended users while separating evidence from judgement and uncertainty.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK', 'MAGENTA_BOOK', 'AEA_COMPETENCIES', 'AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES', 'CDC_EVALUATION_ACTION_GUIDE']::text[], '[{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AEA_COMPETENCIES","title":"AEA Evaluator Competencies","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Competencies-Standards/AEA-Evaluator-Competencies","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"CDC_EVALUATION_ACTION_GUIDE","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework Action Guide","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework-action-guide/","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"CDC_EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework/index.html","locator":"Evaluation Steps: assess context; describe the program; focus evaluation questions and design; gather credible evidence; generate and support conclusions; act on findings. The framework page identifies these steps as its evaluation process.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","locator":"Sections 2.2.1-2.2.2 on understanding an intervention, theory of change and evaluation purpose/questions; survey sampling section describes probability/non-probability sampling, representativeness and non-response; methods chapters cover evaluation design and evidence.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AEA_COMPETENCIES","title":"AEA Evaluator Competencies","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Competencies-Standards/AEA-Evaluator-Competencies","locator":"Competency domains include methodology, context, planning/management and interpersonal practice; interpersonal domain names communication, facilitation and conflict resolution. The page describes a professional competency framework.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","locator":"Guiding Principles page and Systematic Inquiry principle: data-based, thorough, methodical and contextually relevant inquiry; the five principles also include competence, integrity, respect for people, and common good/equity.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"CDC_EVALUATION_ACTION_GUIDE","title":"CDC Program Evaluation Framework Action Guide","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework-action-guide/","locator":"P