('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'method', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:quantitative-analysis-choice', 'Use a quantitative analysis workflow only when the design supports it', 'A quantitative route for preparing, analysing and reporting numeric programme or survey evidence with assumptions and uncertainty visible.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: Optional analysis path only when measurement, sample and design support quantitative analysis; qualitative or descriptive alternatives may fit better.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'Optional analysis path only when measurement, sample and design support quantitative analysis; qualitative or descriptive alternatives may fit better.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['MAGENTA_BOOK', 'SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT', 'NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24', 'DATACARPENTRY_R_SOCIALSCI']::text[], '[{"id":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"DATACARPENTRY_R_SOCIALSCI","title":"R for Social Scientists","url":"https://datacarpentry.github.io/r-socialsci/","region":null,"evidenceType":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"MAGENTA_BOOK","title":"Magenta Book: Central Government guidance on evaluation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-magenta-book/magenta-book-central-government-guidance-on-evaluation-html","locator":"Sections 2.2.1-2.2.2 on understanding an intervention, theory of change and evaluation purpose/questions; survey sampling section describes probability/non-probability sampling, representativeness and non-response; methods chapters cover evaluation design and evidence.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL_2023_24","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey, Panel 2023-2024, Wave 5","url":"https://microdata.nigerianstat.gov.ng/index.php/catalog/82","locator":"Catalogue sections Identification, Version, Scope and Sampling: nationally representative panel of about 5,000 households and six geopolitical zones; household geographic-area identification, migration, labour, education and other modules; anonymized public-distribution dataset metadata.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"DATACARPENTRY_R_SOCIALSCI","title":"R for Social Scientists","url":"https://datacarpentry.github.io/r-socialsci/","locator":"Learner lesson episodes: Starting with Data; Data Wrangling with dplyr/tidyr; Data Visualisation with ggplot2. The lesson description specifies an introductory R workflow for social-science data; its materials state alpha/under-development status.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'nigeria_to_global', '["Software output does not repair confounding, weak measurement, missingness or causal overclaiming.","A statistically significant result is not automatically important or causal.","A reproducible workflow does not repair biased sampling, invalid measures, confounding or unsupported causal claims; the Carpentries lesson is marked alpha.","Optional analysis path only when measurement, sample and design support quantitative analysis; qualitative or descriptive alternatives may fit better."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://datacarpentry.github.io/r-socialsci/', 'R for Social Scientists', '{"source_id":"DATACARPENTRY_R_SOCIALSCI","title":"R for Social Scientists","publisher":"The Carpentries / Data Carpentry","url":"https://datacarpentry.github.io/r-socialsci/","locator":"Learner lesson episodes: Starting with Data; Data Wrangling with dplyr/tidyr; Data Visualisation with ggplot2. The lesson description specifies an introductory R workflow for social-science data; its materials state alpha/under-development status.","what_it_teaches":"Magenta Book links evidence and design to evaluation questions; textbook Chapters 14-15 cover descriptive and inferential analysis; Data Carpentry provides a free social-science data import, cleaning and visualization workflow.","accessed":"2026-10-12","access_cost":"Free lesson materials","limits":"Optional software workflow; lesson is marked alpha and does not select a research design or establish statistical validity."}'::jsonb, '2026-10-12', 'medium', '{"url":"https://datacarpentry.github.io/r-socialsci/","locator":"Learner lesson episodes: Starting with Data; Data Wrangling with dplyr/tidyr; Data Visualisation with ggplot2. The lesson description specifies an introductory R workflow for social-science data; its materials state alpha/under-development status.","supports":"Magenta Book links evidence and design to evaluation questions; textbook Chapters 14-15 cover descrip