('subgroup', 'D078:social-research-evaluation', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078:social-research-evaluation:qualitative-coding-options', 'NVivo or Taguette for documented qualitative coding', 'Software options for organising, highlighting/coding, retrieving and exporting qualitative material after the method and codebook are chosen.', 'This is a D078 area-level addition or route-specific option, not automatically a shared domain foundation. Do not claim that the selected programme teaches this item unless programme curriculum/outcome evidence supports that exact claim; otherwise label it domain/area enrichment. Route note: NVivo is commercial and Taguette is a free alternative; neither chooses codes or validates an interpretation.', NULL, 'useful_later', 'NVivo is commercial and Taguette is a free alternative; neither chooses codes or validates an interpretation.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['TAGUETTE_GETTING_STARTED', 'AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES', 'SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT']::text[], '[{"id":"TAGUETTE_GETTING_STARTED","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","region":null,"evidenceType":null},{"id":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","region":null,"evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"TAGUETTE_GETTING_STARTED","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","locator":"Start a project, upload materials, highlight/tag passages and export tags, highlights, codebooks, documents and project; supports a basic documented coding workflow.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AEA_GUIDING_PRINCIPLES","title":"Guiding Principles for Evaluators","url":"https://www.eval.org/About/Guiding-Principles","locator":"Guiding Principles page and Systematic Inquiry principle: data-based, thorough, methodical and contextually relevant inquiry; the five principles also include competence, integrity, respect for people, and common good/equity.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"SOCIAL_SCIENCE_RESEARCH_TEXT","title":"Social Science Research: Principles, Methods and Practices, revised edition","url":"https://usq.pressbooks.pub/socialscienceresearch/","locator":"Table of contents: Chapter 3 The research process; 5 Research design; 6 Measurement of constructs; 7 Scale reliability and validity; 8 Sampling; 9 Survey research; 11 Case research; 12 Interpretive research; 13 Qualitative analysis; 14-15 quantitative analysis; 16 Research ethics. Online text and downloads are listed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"TAGUETTE_GETTING_STARTED","title":"Getting started with Taguette","url":"https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html","locator":"Start a project, upload materials, highlight/tag passages and export tags, highlights, codebooks, documents and project; supports a basic documented coding workflow.","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Software does not choose codes, make themes true, establish representativeness or replace researcher interpretation.","NVivo licence/version and Taguette hosting/security must be checked.","Coding software organizes material; it does not choose a method, make themes true, establish representativeness or replace researcher interpretation. Check hosting, confidentiality and licence terms.","NVivo is commercial and Taguette is a free alternative; neither chooses codes or validates an interpretation."]'::jsonb, 'source_supported_synthesis', 'medium', 'source_backed', 'linked', 'https://www.taguette.org/getting-started.html', 'Getting started with Taguette', '{"source_id":"TAGUETTE_GETTING_STARTED","title":"Getting started with Taguette","publisher":"Taguette project","url":"https://w