ntroduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","region":"Global educational resource","evidenceType":null}],"source_locators":[{"sourceId":"UNESCO_ISCED","title":"ISCED Fields of Education and Training 2013: Detailed Field Descriptions","url":"https://uis.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2025/04/international-standard-classification-of-education-fields-of-education-and-training-2013-detailed-field-descriptions-2015-en.pdf","locator":"Fields 0311–0314 and adjacent inclusion/exclusion notes for economics, political science, psychology, sociology/cultural studies, demography and social geography","claimRole":"contextual_use"},{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","locator":"Research process, method selection, reliability/validity, ethics and social research methods","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078-SOC-THEORY-CONTEXT"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free learning resource; review the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'sociology-social-anthropology', 'useful', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Use concepts to make a reasoned interpretation of an observed pattern, compare explanations, and identify what evidence would support or challenge each account; output a concept-to-evidence explanation rather than name-dropping a theory. Guardrail: A framework can direct attention but may also obscure evidence that does not fit it. Theory does not by itself establish an empirical claim.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-SOC-ETHICS-REFLEXIVITY', 'Research ethics, consent, and reflexivity in social inquiry', 'The ability to anticipate how research affects people, seek appropriate consent/permissions, protect privacy, document the researcher�s position, and respond to ethical issues throughout the study.', 'Human relationships, community settings, sensitive identities, and digital traces make these decisions integral to sociological and anthropological fieldwork; the same broad ethics foundation supports other D078 routes, while specific approvals vary by institution and jurisdiction. Produce an ethics and data-handling plan that explains participation, confidentiality, risk, recording, storage, and how the researcher�s role may shape access and interpretation. No claim that a curriculum confers research approval or ethics certification. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produce an ethics and data-handling plan that explains participation, confidentiality, risk, recording, storage, and how the researcher�s role may shape access and interpretation. Guardrail: AAA guidance is professional guidance, not Nigerian law. Nigeria�s National Code is specifically a health-research code; do not apply it as a blanket rule to every social-science project without checking institutional scope.', 'Produce an ethics and data-handling plan that explains participation, confidentiality, risk, recording, storage, and how the researcher�s role may shape access and interpretation.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produce an ethics and data-handling plan that explains participation, confidentiality, risk, recording, storage, and how the researcher�s role may shape access and interpretation. Guardrail: AAA guidance is professional guidance, not Nigerian law. Nigeria�s National Code is specifically a health-research code; do not apply it as a blanket rule to every social-science project without checking institutional scope.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAA_ETHICS', 'NHREC_CODE_SCOPE', 'UNESCO_GENAI', 'AAA_CONSENT', 'UKDS_RDM']::text[], '[{"id":"AAA_ETHICS","title":"Principles of Professional Responsibility / Code of Ethics","url":"https://americananthro.org/wp-content/uploads/ethicscode-2.pdf","region":"Professional guidance; global, with local law/community obligations","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NHREC_CODE_SCOPE","title":"National Code of Health Research Ethics","url":"https://nhrec.net/nhrec/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/NCHRE_Aug_07.pdf","region":"Nigeria; health research ethics code","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UNESCO_GENAI","title":"Guidance for generative AI in education and research","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/guidance-generative-ai-education-and-research","region":"International guidance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AAA_CONSENT","title":"Obtain Informed Consent and Necessary Permissions","url":"https://ethics.americananthro.org/ethics-statement-3-obtain-informed-consent-and-necessary-permissions/","region":"Professional guidance; local rules vary","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UKDS_RDM","title":"Foundations of research data management","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/data-producer-support/foundations-of-research-data-management/","region":"Global learning resource","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AAA_ETHICS","title":"Principles of Professional Responsibility / Code of Ethics","url":"https://americananthro.org/wp-content/uploads/ethicscode-2.pdf","locator":"Researcher responsibilities, ethical relationships, obligations to people/communities, and local laws/codes","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NISER_METHODS","title":"Research Methodology Training","url":"https://niser.gov.ng/v2/research-methodology-training/","lo