('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-ETHNOGRAPHIC-FIELDWORK', 'Ethnographic fieldwork and participant observation', 'A sustained way of learning about social life by observing practices and interactions in context, often alongside conversations and documentary evidence.', 'A core social-anthropological route when meanings and practices are best understood in everyday settings; it is not required for every sociological study. Keep dated, contextual field notes that distinguish what was observed, what participants said, and the researcher�s interpretation; develop an account of practice and setting. Not asserted as a programme outcome without a specific curriculum link. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Keep dated, contextual field notes that distinguish what was observed, what participants said, and the researcher�s interpretation; develop an account of practice and setting. Guardrail: Researcher presence and position can affect what is seen and said. One case cannot automatically represent a wider population.', 'Keep dated, contextual field notes that distinguish what was observed, what participants said, and the researcher�s interpretation; develop an account of practice and setting.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Keep dated, contextual field notes that distinguish what was observed, what participants said, and the researcher�s interpretation; develop an account of practice and setting. Guardrail: Researcher presence and position can affect what is seen and said. One case cannot automatically represent a wider population.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAA_FIELDWORK', 'UNESCO_ISCED', 'OPENSTAX_METHODS', 'OPEN_ANTHRO_FIELDWORK']::text[], '[{"id":"AAA_FIELDWORK","title":"How to Hold a Workshop 