ute. Task: Deploy an already-designed questionnaire to collect structured field responses; export a documented dataset for checking and analysis. Guardrail: The platform cannot make a biased sample representative or a weak question valid. Offline syncing, device access, language, consent, privacy, and project account settings must be checked.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-THEMATIC-ANALYSIS', 'Thematic/framework analysis with an auditable codebook', 'A systematic way to label and compare material so a researcher can explain recurring patterns, differences, and exceptions in relation to the question.', 'Supports interpretation of social accounts and documents without reducing qualitative analysis to counting words or treating themes as self-evident. Develop and revise codes, record definitions and examples, compare cases, and produce a theme/evidence matrix with supporting excerpts and disconfirming cases. Not claimed as programme-taught unless specific curriculum material supports it. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Develop and revise codes, record definitions and examples, compare cases, and produce a theme/evidence matrix with supporting excerpts and disconfirming cases. Guardrail: Coding does not eliminate interpretation or researcher influence. Do not claim inter-coder reliability as universally appropriate across all qualitative traditions.', 'Develop and revise codes, record definitions and examples, compare cases, and produce a theme/evidence matrix with supporting excerpts and disconfirming cases.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Develop and revise codes, record definitions and examples, compare cases, and produce a theme/evidence matrix with supporting excerpts and disconfirming cases. Guardrail: Coding does not eliminate interpretation or researcher influence. Do not claim inter-coder reliability as universally appropriate across all qualitative traditions.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_QUALITATIVE', 'OPENSTAX_METHODS']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_QUALITATIVE","title":"Qualitative data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/qualitative-data/","region":"Global learning resource; UK collection examples","evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","region":"Global educational resource","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_QUALITATIVE","title":"Qualitative data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/qualitative-data/","locator":"Types of qualitative evidence, lived experience, mixed evidence, reuse and teaching resources","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","locator":"Research process, method selection, reliability/validity, ethics and social research methods","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UKDS_QUALITATIVE","title":"Qualitative data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/qualitative-data/","locator":"Types of qualitative evidence, lived experience, mixed evidence, reuse and teaching resources","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","locator":"Research process, method selection, reliability/validity, ethics and social research methods","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","locator":"Research process, method selection, reliability/validity, ethics and social research methods","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resource"}]'::jsonb, 'global', '["Coding does not eliminate interpretation or researcher influence.","Do not claim inter-coder reliability as universally appropriate across 