('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-SECONDARY-QUAL-ANALYSIS', 'Secondary qualitative-data analysis and provenance assessment', 'Re-analysis of qualitative material collected in an earlier project to answer a new or related question, with attention to the original study context and sampling.', 'Allows sociologists and anthropologists to study social change or compare accounts without always collecting new data, where accessible data and ethics permit. Review catalogue, instruments, sample and field context; select relevant cases; document how new concepts or comparisons relate to the original data; produce a bounded re-analysis. A self-directed additional method unless programme evidence establishes otherwise. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Review catalogue, instruments, sample and field context; select relevant cases; document how new concepts or comparisons relate to the original data; produce a bounded re-analysis. Guardrail: Original data may not contain the concepts or detail needed for the new question. Re-use can be constrained by consent, disclosure risk, access, and data quality.', 'Review catalogue, instruments, sample and field context; select relevant cases; document how new concepts or comparisons relate to the original data; produce a bounded re-analysis.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Review catalogue, instruments, sample and field context; select relevant cases; document how new concepts or comparisons relate to the original data; produce a bounded re-analysis. Guardrail: Original data may not contain the concepts or detail needed for the new question. Re-use can be constrained by consent, disclosure risk, access, and data quality.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_QUALITA