('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-DOCUMENT-ANALYSIS', 'Systematic document and media analysis', 'A planned way to examine documents or media as evidence about institutions, categories, public narratives, or social change.', 'Useful where social institutions and public discourse leave documentary evidence; interpretation must consider authorship, audience, historical context, and missing voices. Define a corpus and selection rules, note who produced each source and for what purpose, analyze content/meaning, and keep a source-to-claim trail. No claim of direct programme teaching. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Define a corpus and selection rules, note who produced each source and for what purpose, analyze content/meaning, and keep a source-to-claim trail. Guardrail: Documents do not transparently mirror social reality. Digitized corpus selection and OCR can produce coverage and measurement bias.', 'Define a corpus and selection rules, note who produced each source and for what purpose, analyze content/meaning, and keep a source-to-claim trail.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Define a corpus and selection rules, note who produced each source and for what purpose, analyze content/meaning, and keep a source-to-claim trail. Guardrail: Documents do not transparently mirror social reality. Digitized corpus selection and OCR can produce coverage and measurement bias.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_QUALITATIVE', 'GOVUK_DOCUMENT_ANALYSIS', 'OPENSTAX_METHODS']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_QUALITATIVE","title":"Qualitative data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/qualitative-data/","region":"Global learning resource; UK collection examples","evidenceType":null},{"id":"GOVUK_DOCUMENT_ANALYSIS","title":"Guidance on qualitative research methods (document analysis section)","url":"https://acss.food.gov.uk/QAT5","region":"United Kingdom guidance; method explanation broader","evidenceType":null},{"id":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","region":"Global educational resource","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_QUALITATIVE","title":"Qualitative data","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/qualitative-data/","locator":"Types of qualitative evidence, lived experience, mixed evidence, reuse and teaching resources","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"GOVUK_DOCUMENT_ANALYSIS","title":"Guidance on qualitative research methods (document analysis section)","url":"https://acss.food.gov.uk/QAT5","locator":"Explains document analysis and when existing qualitative documents can be useful; compare interviews/focus groups for in-depth views","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"GOVUK_DOCUMENT_ANALYSIS","title":"Guidance on qualitative research methods (document analysis section)","url":"https://acss.food.gov.uk/QAT5","locator":"Explains document analysis and when existing qualitative documents can be useful; compare interviews/focus groups for in-depth views","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_METHODS","title":"Introduction to Sociology 3e, Research Methods section summary","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-section-summary","locator":"Research process, method selection, reliability/validity, ethics and social research methods","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"GOVUK_DOCUMENT_ANALYSIS","title":"Guidance on qualitative research methods (document analysis section)","url":"https://acss.food.gov.uk/QAT5","locator":"Explains document analysis and when existing qualitative documents can be useful; compare interviews/focus groups for in-depth views","claimRole":"task_specific_learning_resourc