('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-SURVEY-DESIGN', 'Social survey design, sampling, and question pretesting', 'A method for deciding who a survey should represent, how people will be selected, how concepts become answerable questions, and how to test that questions are understood as intended.', 'Used in sociology and social anthropology when the question calls for comparable reports across people or communities; it does not replace ethnography or make a survey representative by itself. Produce a sampling/instrument plan that records the target population, sample selection, measurement definitions, question wording, pilot findings and known sources of survey error. A D078 area learning addition; programme teaching is not asserted without separate curriculum evidence. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produce a sampling/instrument plan that records the target population, sample selection, measurement definitions, question wording, pilot findings and known sources of survey error. Guardrail: Convenience or poorly covered samples do not support population-representative claims. Translation and local-language equivalence need review and testing with intended respondents.', 'Produce a sampling/instrument plan that records the target population, sample selection, measurement definitions, question wording, pilot findings and known sources of survey error.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produce a sampling/instrument plan that records the target population, sample selection, measurement definitions, question wording, pilot findings and known sources of survey error. Guardrail: Convenience or poorly covered samples do not support population-representative claims. Translation and local-language equivalence need review and testing with intended respondents.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_SURVEY_DATA', 'UKDS_SURVEY_TRAINING', 'AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES', 'NASA_NIGERIA']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_SURVEY_DATA","title":"Survey data: methods, software, weights and design","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/survey-data/","region":"United Kingdom data service; methods transferable, examples/data are UK-specific","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UKDS_SURVEY_TRAINING","title":"Introduction to survey data","url":"https://repository.ncrm.ac.uk/resources/online/all/intro_survey_data","region":"United Kingdom educational resource; methods globally applicable with dataset-specific adaptation","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","region":"Professional survey-research guidance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NASA_NIGERIA","title":"Association overview and objectives","url":"https://www.nasanigeria.org.ng/","region":"Nigeria professional association; claims are attributed to the association itself","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_SURVEY_DATA","title":"Survey data: methods, software, weights and design","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/survey-data/","locator":"Survey weights/complex samples, survey documentation, software guides including R/SPSS/Stata, and short videos on weights and documentation","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UKDS_SURVEY_TRAINING","title":"Introduction to survey data","url":"https://repository.ncrm.ac.uk/resources/online/all/intro_survey_data","locator":"Free interactive learning units include survey weights, sampling, precision and confidence intervals","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","locator":"Question wording, cognitive pretesting, piloting, survey quality and reporting guidanc