 mastery checkpoint. Task: Produce a sampling/instrument plan that records the target population, sample selection, measurement definitions, question wording, pilot findings and known sources of survey error. Guardrail: Convenience or poorly covered samples do not support population-representative claims. Translation and local-language equivalence need review and testing with intended respondents.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-SURVEY-ANALYSIS-R', 'Design-aware analysis of social survey data (R or documented alternatives)', 'A way to summarize and compare survey responses while using the dataset''s supplied weights, strata, clusters and other design information when required.', 'This supports quantitative sociology/social anthropology for population patterns and group comparisons; R is one available implementation, not the method itself or a universal prerequisite. Read the survey documentation, identify the correct analysis variables, create weighted estimates with suitable uncertainty calculations, and produce a reproducible result with a population and dataset scope note. No claim that D078 or a chosen programme teaches R or confers data-analysis competence. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Read the survey documentation, identify the correct analysis variables, create weighted estimates with suitable uncertainty calculations, and produce a reproducible result with a population and dataset scope note. Guardrail: A package cannot repair missing coverage, poor measurement, or undocumented design. The UK examples are not Nigerian survey instructions; use the Nigerian dataset''s own documentation and weights.', 'Read the survey documentation, identify the correct analysis variables, create weighted estimates with suitable uncertainty calculations, and produce a reproducible result with a population and dataset scope note.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Read the survey documentation, identify the correct analysis variables, create weighted estimates with suitable uncertainty calculations, and produce a reproducible result with a population and dataset scope note. Guardrail: A package cannot repair missing coverage, poor measurement, or undocumented design. The UK examples are not Nigerian survey instructions; use the Nigerian dataset''s own documentation and weights.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_R_SURVEY_GUIDE', 'R_SURVEY_PACKAGE', 'NBS_GHS_PANEL', 'UKDS_SURVEY_DATA']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_R_SURVEY_GUIDE","title":"Analysing social survey data using R","url":"https://ukdataserviceopen.github.io/UKDS_RGuide/","region":"UK data example; open methods teaching for global learners","evidenceType":null},{"id":"R_SURVEY_PACKAGE","title":"survey: analysis of complex survey samples documentation","url":"https://cran.r-project.org/package=survey","region":"Global open-source software documentation","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NBS_GHS_PANEL","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey Panel","url":"https://www.nigerianstat.gov.ng/download/388","region":"Nigeria official statistical survey; survey rounds and access terms vary","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UKDS_SURVEY_DATA","title":"Survey data: methods, software, weights and design","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/survey-data/","region":"United Kingdom data service; methods transferable, examples/data are UK-specific","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_R_SURVEY_GUIDE","title":"Analysing social survey data using R","url":"https://ukdataserviceopen.github.io/UKDS_RGuide/","locator":"2024 guide; importing social survey data, descriptive tabulations, survey weights and design variables; examples use British Social Attitudes Survey 2017","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"R_SURVEY_PACKAGE","title":"survey: analysis of complex survey samples documentation","url":"https://cran.r-project.org/package=survey","locator":"Package reference and vignettes for weighted estimates, stratified/clustered designs, replicate weights, and variance estimation","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NBS_GHS_PANEL","title":"Nigeria General Household Survey Panel","url":"https://www.nigerianstat.gov.ng/download/388","locator":"Survey descri