('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-AI-SURVEY-QUESTION-DRAFTING', 'Human-reviewed AI assistance for survey question drafting', 'A bounded workflow in which a generative AI system suggests or edits survey wording, while researchers retain responsibility for the construct, language, measurement quality and final instrument.', 'May speed early drafting for a sociology survey, but it does not show that the wording measures social experience accurately or works across Nigerian languages and communities. Compare a documented AI suggestion with the intended concept, have subject and language-competent reviewers check it, then cognitively pretest it with people from the intended respondent group; output includes prompt/model/version notes, revisions and pretest findings. Optional emerging area enrichment; no programme teaching or local-language performance is claimed. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Compare a documented AI suggestion with the intended concept, have subject and language-competent reviewers check it, then cognitively pretest it with people from the intended respondent group; output includes prompt/model/version notes, revisions and pretest findings. Guardrail: AAPOR guidance is professional survey guidance, not proof that a particular AI model or translation is valid. Do not input confidential participant data into an unapproved system.', 'Compare a documented AI suggestion with the intended concept, have subject and language-competent reviewers check it, then cognitively pretest it with people from the intended respondent group; output includes prompt/model/version notes, revisions and pretest findings.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Compare a documented AI suggestion with the intended concept, have subject and language-competent reviewers check it, then cognitively pretest it with people from the intended respondent group; output includes prompt/model/version notes, revisions and pretest findings. Guardrail: AAPOR guidance is professional survey guidance, not proof that a particular AI model or translation is valid. Do not input confidential participant data into an unapproved system.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_2026', 'AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES']::text[], '[{"id":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Survey-Research.pdf","region":"Professional survey-research guidance; U.S.-based association with broad methodological relevance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","region":"Professional survey-research guidance","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_2026","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Survey-Research.pdf","locator":"2026 report; section 3.4 pp.25–27 on question writing/editing/translation; sections 3–6 and pp.30–67 discuss evaluation, human oversight, disclosure and participant protections","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","locator":"Question wording, cognitive pretesting, piloting, survey quality and reporting guidance","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AAPOR_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","locator":"Question wording, cognitive pretesting, piloting, survey quality and reporting guidance","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"AAPOR_RESPONSIBLE_AI_2026","title":"Responsib