('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'competency', 'D078-SOC-DIGITAL-TRACE-ETHICS', 'Digital trace data provenance, access, and ethics', 'The ability to explain how online traces were created, whose activity they represent, what platform/API conditions filtered them, and whether their research use is ethical and permitted.', 'Digital interaction is social activity, but trace availability is shaped by platform design, unequal access, moderation, and researcher collection choices. Write a data-source and access log covering platform, collection time, inclusion/exclusion, API or terms, personal-data risk, consent/expectation, and known coverage gaps. Not assumed to be part of curriculum. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Write a data-source and access log covering platform, collection time, inclusion/exclusion, API or terms, personal-data risk, consent/expectation, and known coverage gaps. Guardrail: Publicly visible data are not automatically ethically free to republish or expose. Representativeness and platform access may be unknown.', 'Write a data-source and access log covering platform, collection time, inclusion/exclusion, API or terms, personal-data risk, consent/expectation, and known coverage gaps.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Write a data-source and access log covering platform, collection time, inclusion/exclusion, API or terms, personal-data risk, consent/expectation, and known coverage gaps. Guardrail: Publicly visible data are not automatically ethically free to republish or expose. Representativeness and platform access may be unknown.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL', 'AAA_ETHICS', 'UNESCO_GENAI', 'UKDS_DATA_SKILLS']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL","title":"Computational social science","url":"https://ukdata