('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'tool', 'D078-SOC-QUANT-TEXT-R', 'Quantitative text analysis in R (quanteda) or Python (NLTK/spaCy alternatives)', 'A computational workflow that turns a documented text corpus into analyzable units/features for comparison, classification, scaling, or pattern exploration; quanteda is an R package with task-specific corpus and text-analysis functions.', 'Can support analysis of large collections of speeches, public documents, or consented posts, but concepts such as sentiment or topic need substantive validation in context and language. Build a corpus with source metadata, tokenize consistently, document exclusions and preprocessing, test measures against known examples, and produce a reproducible analysis table or plot. Optional advanced route; no programme-specific software teaching asserted. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Build a corpus with source metadata, tokenize consistently, document exclusions and preprocessing, test measures against known examples, and produce a reproducible analysis table or plot. Guardrail: Language varieties, multilingual text, irony, code-switching, and platform context affect validity. Tokenization or model output does not measure a social concept without construct validation.', 'Build a corpus with source metadata, tokenize consistently, document exclusions and preprocessing, test measures against known examples, and produce a reproducible analysis table or plot.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Build a corpus with source metadata, tokenize consistently, document exclusions and preprocessing, test measures against known examples, and produce a reproducible analysis table or plot. Guardrail: Language varieties, multilingual text, irony, code-switching, and platform context affect validity. Tokenization or model output does not measure a social concept without construct validation.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL', 'NELSON_LLM_CODING_2025', 'QUANTEDA_TUTORIALS']::text[], '[{"id":"UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL","title":"Computational social science","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/computational-social-science/","region":"Global learning resource; platform access varies","evidenceType":null},{"id":"NELSON_LLM_CODING_2025","title":"Updating ‘The Future of Coding’: Qualitative Coding with Generative Large Language Models","url":"https://www.lauraknelson.com/publication/updating-the-future-of-coding/","region":"International scholarly research","evidenceType":null},{"id":"QUANTEDA_TUTORIALS","title":"Quanteda tutorials: text analysis with R","url":"https://tutorials.quanteda.io/","region":"Global open learning resource","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL","title":"Computational social science","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/computational-social-science/","locator":"Resources on social media data, text-mining, web-scraping/APIs, data handling, sentiment analysis; explicit note that platform/API demonstrations may become outdated","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"NELSON_LLM_CODING_2025","title":"Updating ‘The Future of Coding’: Qualitative Coding with Generative Large Language Models","url":"https://www.lauraknelson.com/publication/updating-the-future-of-coding/","locator":"2025 article summary on computational methods and LLMs for qualitative text coding","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"QUANTEDA_TUTORIALS","title":"Quanteda tutorials: text analysis with R","url":"https://tutorials.quanteda.io/","locator":"R introduction, corpus, tokens, document-feature matrix, text scaling, classification and topic models","claimRole":null},{"sourceId":"UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL","title":"Computational social science","url":"https://ukdataservice.ac.uk/learning-hub/computational-social-science/","locat