_LLM_CODING_2025","title":"Updating ‘The Future of Coding’: Qualitative Coding with Generative Large Language Models","url":"https://www.lauraknelson.com/publication/updating-the-future-of-coding/","locator":"2025 article summary on computational methods and LLMs for qualitative text coding","claimRole":"contextual_use"}]}},"reviewed_by":"local_d078_item_disposition","decision_id":"D078-SOC-QUANT-TEXT-R"}'::jsonb, 'free_task_specific_learning_resource', NULL, 'English', 'Free learning resource; review the provider''s current access terms.', NULL, 'area_specific_enrichment_candidate', 'Area specific enrichment candidate', 'sociology-social-anthropology', 'optional', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Build a corpus with source metadata, tokenize consistently, document exclusions and preprocessing, test measures against known examples, and produce a reproducible analysis table or plot. Guardrail: Language varieties, multilingual text, irony, code-switching, and platform context affect validity. Tokenization or model output does not measure a social concept without construct validation.'),
('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'D078-SOC-LLM-SYNTHETIC-PILOT', 'LLM-generated synthetic respondents for pilot testing (not human evidence)', 'An experimental use of language models to generate simulated responses or probe whether a questionnaire/intervention prompt is understandable before a real study.', 'May help generate hypotheses or surface wording issues; synthetic outputs do not represent Nigerian or any real population and cannot stand in for sampled participants or validate estimates. A clearly labelled pilot artifact listing prompts, model/version, generated variation, failure cases, and revisions to test with actual people or established pretesting methods. Exploratory research literacy only, not a recommended substitute for field research. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: A clearly labelled pilot artifact listing prompts, model/version, generated variation, failure cases, and revisions to test with actual people or established pretesting methods. Guardrail: LLM outputs can compress real-world diversity and reflect training data stereotypes. Synthetic responses are not sample data and must not be used to claim prevalence or treatment effects.', 'A clearly labelled pilot artifact listing prompts, model/version, generated variation, failure cases, and revisions to test with actual people or established pretesting methods.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: A clearly labelled pilot artifact listing prompts, model/version, generated variation, failure cases, and revisions to test with actual people or established pretesting methods. Guardrail: LLM outputs can compress real-world diversity and reflect training data stereotypes. Synthetic responses are not sample data and must not be used to claim prevalence or treatment effects.', 