('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'SOC-M1', 'Qualitative interviewing and contextual observation', 'Ways of gathering detailed accounts or observing activity in its setting using a planned, ethical procedure.', 'A sociology/social anthropology method choice when the question concerns meaning, process or context. Produces situated evidence about how people experience relationships, institutions and everyday practices. Programme-specific mapping remains unasserted pending course/outcome crosswalk. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produces situated evidence about how people experience relationships, institutions and everyday practices. Guardrail: Does not automatically estimate prevalence or causality; researcher position and access shape evidence.', 'Produces situated evidence about how people experience relationships, institutions and everyday practices.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Produces situated evidence about how people experience relationships, institutions and everyday practices. Guardrail: Does not automatically estimate prevalence or causality; researcher position and access shape evidence.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['OPENSTAX_SOCIOLOGY_METHODS', 'ONET_SOCIOLOGISTS']::text[], '[{"id":"OPENSTAX_SOCIOLOGY_METHODS","title":"OpenStax Introduction to Sociology 3e, Sociological Research","url":"https://openstax.org/books/introduction-sociology-3e/pages/2-introduction","region":"Open educational resource; global use","evidenceType":null},{"id":"ONET_SOCIOLOGISTS","title":"O*NET OnLine: Sociologists, 19-3041.00","url":"https://www.onetonline.org/link/details/19-3041.00","region":"United States occupational evidence","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"OPENSTAX_SOCIOLOGY_METHODS","tit