('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'competency', 'SOC-C2', 'Reflexive, auditable interpretation', 'Ability to show how evidence supports an interpretation, examine alternative explanations and keep a traceable account of analytic choices.', 'A quality competency for interpretive sociological work, especially when tools or AI assist analysis. Makes a report explain what was inferred and what remains uncertain, rather than presenting a theme or model output as self-evident fact. Programme mapping is not asserted absent direct reviewed evidence. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Makes a report explain what was inferred and what remains uncertain, rather than presenting a theme or model output as self-evident fact. Guardrail: Reflexivity cannot eliminate bias or compensate for weak/irrelevant evidence.', 'Makes a report explain what was inferred and what remains uncertain, rather than presenting a theme or model output as self-evident fact.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Makes a report explain what was inferred and what remains uncertain, rather than presenting a theme or model output as self-evident fact. Guardrail: Reflexivity cannot eliminate bias or compensate for weak/irrelevant evidence.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['TUM_CSS_LLM', 'APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY', 'SICSS_CURRICULUM']::text[], '[{"id":"TUM_CSS_LLM","title":"TUM Computational Social Science: Data and Methods","url":"https://www.hfp.tum.de/en/css/forschung/data-methods/","region":"Global research method context; German institution","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY","title":"Guidance on use of artificial intelligence in submissions to Qualitative Psychology","url":"https://www.apa.org/pubs/journals/qua/ai-policy","region":"Journal policy; not 