('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'tool', 'SOC-T1', 'Python or R for computational social-science text workflows', 'Programming environments and libraries used to retrieve permitted text data, prepare it consistently, apply transparent analysis and preserve executable steps.', 'A selectable computational route for sociological text/digital-trace research, not a universal sociology requirement. Can support larger or repeatable text tasks such as classification, named-entity extraction or topic exploration when design justifies computation. No programme teaches this unless specific curriculum evidence confirms it; treat as optional enrichment otherwise. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Can support larger or repeatable text tasks such as classification, named-entity extraction or topic exploration when design justifies computation. Guardrail: Models can encode language and sample bias; online texts are not representative by default; platform APIs and terms change.', 'Can support larger or repeatable text tasks such as classification, named-entity extraction or topic exploration when design justifies computation.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Can support larger or repeatable text tasks such as classification, named-entity extraction or topic exploration when design justifies computation. Guardrail: Models can encode language and sample bias; online texts are not representative by default; platform APIs and terms change.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['SGSSS_TEXT_ANALYSIS', 'UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL']::text[], '[{"id":"SGSSS_TEXT_ANALYSIS","title":"Practical Computational Methods for Social Scientists: Text Analysis","url":"https://github.com/SGSSSonline/text-analysis","region":"Global learning resource; UK provider","evidenceType":null},{"id":"UKDS_COM