('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'SOC-S1', 'Text preparation and computational text analysis', 'Preparing text consistently and using transparent computational procedures to describe or classify features such as terms, topics or named entities.', 'An optional computational method within sociological inquiry; quantitative pattern does not replace meaning/context analysis. Can help examine large document sets or digital traces for patterns, after checking whether the collection represents the intended population or discourse. Not claimed as taught content without curriculum evidence. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Can help examine large document sets or digital traces for patterns, after checking whether the collection represents the intended population or discourse. Guardrail: Topic/sentiment labels are not direct measures of social constructs without validation; language, sarcasm, sampling and platform bias matter.', 'Can help examine large document sets or digital traces for patterns, after checking whether the collection represents the intended population or discourse.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Can help examine large document sets or digital traces for patterns, after checking whether the collection represents the intended population or discourse. Guardrail: Topic/sentiment labels are not direct measures of social constructs without validation; language, sarcasm, sampling and platform bias matter.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['SGSSS_TEXT_ANALYSIS', 'SICSS_CURRICULUM', 'UKDS_COMPUTATIONAL']::text[], '[{"id":"SGSSS_TEXT_ANALYSIS","title":"Practical Computational Methods for Social Scientists: Text Analysis","url":"https://github.com/SGSSSonline/text-analysis","region":"Global learning resource; UK provider","evidenceType":n