('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'SOC-A1', 'Human-validated AI annotation for social research', 'A workflow where an AI model proposes labels for a clearly defined text-coding task and researchers test its output against human-reviewed examples.', 'A contested, emerging aid to a sociological coding workflow, not autonomous analysis or a standard expected for all sociologists. May reduce repetitive first-pass sorting or scale comparison of text when validation shows the model works for that dataset and purpose. Not established as programme-taught content; optional domain/area enrichment only. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: May reduce repetitive first-pass sorting or scale comparison of text when validation shows the model works for that dataset and purpose. Guardrail: Fabrication, bias, unstable outputs, privacy leakage and mismatch to local language/context; researchers retain interpretive responsibility.', 'May reduce repetitive first-pass sorting or scale comparison of text when validation shows the model works for that dataset and purpose.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: May reduce repetitive first-pass sorting or scale comparison of text when validation shows the model works for that dataset and purpose. Guardrail: Fabrication, bias, unstable outputs, privacy leakage and mismatch to local language/context; researchers retain interpretive responsibility.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['TUM_CSS_LLM', 'APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY', 'SICSS_CURRICULUM']::text[], '[{"id":"TUM_CSS_LLM","title":"TUM Computational Social Science: Data and Methods","url":"https://www.hfp.tum.de/en/css/forschung/data-methods/","region":"Global research method context; German institution","evidenceType":null},{"id":"APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY","title":"Guidance on use of a