('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'competency', 'SOC-C3', 'AI research validation and data-governance practice', 'Ability to test AI-assisted outputs against human-reviewed evidence, document model/version and uncertainty, and protect confidential or restricted material.', 'A conditional capability for the emerging AI-assisted research route, not prerequisite for ordinary qualitative work. Prevents model-generated coding, summaries or citations from silently becoming research findings. Not claimed as programme outcome. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Prevents model-generated coding, summaries or citations from silently becoming research findings. Guardrail: Human review does not guarantee neutrality; validation sample may omit groups/languages or rare errors.', 'Prevents model-generated coding, summaries or citations from silently becoming research findings.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Prevents model-generated coding, summaries or citations from silently becoming research findings. Guardrail: Human review does not guarantee neutrality; validation sample may omit groups/languages or rare errors.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY', 'TUM_CSS_LLM', 'SICSS_CURRICULUM']::text[], '[{"id":"APA_QUAL_AI_POLICY","title":"Guidance on use of artificial intelligence in submissions to Qualitative Psychology","url":"https://www.apa.org/pubs/journals/qua/ai-policy","region":"Journal policy; not universal law or all-discipline consensus","evidenceType":null},{"id":"TUM_CSS_LLM","title":"TUM Computational Social Science: Data and Methods","url":"https://www.hfp.tum.de/en/css/forschung/data-methods/","region":"Global research method context; German institution","evidenceType":null},{"id":"SICSS_CURRICULUM","t