('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'SOC-M3', 'Agent-based modelling of social mechanisms', 'A computational method that represents people/groups as agents following explicit rules and studies how interactions may produce aggregate patterns.', 'A specialist, optional sociology/social anthropology simulation route when theory concerns interaction and emergent group-level patterns. Allows researchers to explore the implications of specified mechanisms and assumptions, not to recreate a population automatically. Not claimed as curriculum-taught. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Allows researchers to explore the implications of specified mechanisms and assumptions, not to recreate a population automatically. Guardrail: A plausible simulation is not empirical confirmation or forecast; behavior follows researcher-coded assumptions.', 'Allows researchers to explore the implications of specified mechanisms and assumptions, not to recreate a population automatically.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: Allows researchers to explore the implications of specified mechanisms and assumptions, not to recreate a population automatically. Guardrail: A plausible simulation is not empirical confirmation or forecast; behavior follows researcher-coded assumptions.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['CASEVO_PAPER', 'MESA_FRAMEWORK']::text[], '[{"id":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive Agents and Social Evolution Simulator","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19498","region":"International research preprint","evidenceType":null},{"id":"MESA_FRAMEWORK","title":"Mesa: Agent-based Modeling in Python","url":"https://mesa.readthedocs.io/","region":"Open-source software, global","evidenceType":null}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceId":"CASEVO_PAPER","title":"Casevo: A Cognitive