('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'method', 'SOC-M4', 'AI-assisted survey item drafting/translation with cognitive pretesting', 'A human-led survey-development workflow where AI proposes or edits question wording/translations, followed by subject/language review and testing with intended respondents.', 'Optional emerging method in Sociology when a study uses a survey; not an all-student requirement. Specialist survey-method work may be owned by Social Research and Evaluation, subject to that area review. May speed iteration, while cognitive interviewing identifies whether people understand questions as intended and whether translations preserve construct meaning. Not claimed as programme-taught unless its curriculum contract explicitly includes this activity. Route note: Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: May speed iteration, while cognitive interviewing identifies whether people understand questions as intended and whether translations preserve construct meaning. Guardrail: Fluency does not establish equivalence or validity; AI can introduce bias, leading wording or cultural assumptions. Nigerian language performance needs local pretesting.', 'May speed iteration, while cognitive interviewing identifies whether people understand questions as intended and whether translations preserve construct meaning.', 'useful_later', 'Show only within the selected sociology social anthropology area and relevant use case, as an optional route. Task: May speed iteration, while cognitive interviewing identifies whether people understand questions as intended and whether translations preserve construct meaning. Guardrail: Fluency does not establish equivalence or validity; AI can introduce bias, leading wording or cultural assumptions. Nigerian language performance needs local pretesting.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAPOR_AI_SURVEY', 'AAPOR_SURVEY_BEST_PRACTICES']::text[]