('subgroup', 'D078:sociology-social-anthropology', 'D078', 'competency', 'SOC-C4', 'Cognitive pretesting and translation-equivalence review', 'Ability to examine how intended respondents understand a question, retrieve information and choose an answer, then use this evidence to revise wording/translation.', 'Established survey-quality competency used conditionally when constructing/translating an instrument; not needed on every Sociology route. Finds confusion, mismatched meaning or response-process problems before the larger survey is fielded. No programme mapping claimed without direct reviewed course evidence. Route note: Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Finds confusion, mismatched meaning or response-process problems before the larger survey is fielded. Guardrail: A small pretest can reveal problems but does not alone establish population representativeness, reliability or validity.', 'Finds confusion, mismatched meaning or response-process problems before the larger survey is fielded.', 'build_next', 'Show within the selected sociology social anthropology area as a learner-selectable focus, not a compulsory mastery checkpoint. Task: Finds confusion, mismatched meaning or response-process problems before the larger survey is fielded. Guardrail: A small pretest can reveal problems but does not alone establish population representativeness, reliability or validity.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['AAPOR_SURVEY_BEST_PRACTICES', 'AAPOR_AI_SURVEY']::text[], '[{"id":"AAPOR_SURVEY_BEST_PRACTICES","title":"AAPOR Best Practices for Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/standards-and-ethics/best-practices/","region":"Professional guidance; U.S. association; general method relevance","evidenceType":null},{"id":"AAPOR_AI_SURVEY","title":"Responsible AI Integration in Survey Research","url":"https://aapor.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Responsible-AI-Integration-In-Surv